\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Unchanged as Government Measures Limit Volatility\b0\par\par\uc2 456 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 2012\par 22:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  real steady ahead of Bernanke testimony\par \par \uc2 --Government \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  limit exchange volatility\par \par \uc2 --Real exits active trading at BRL2.0351 to the dollar\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Brian Asher \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RIO DE JANEIRO--The Brazilian real was unchanged Monday as investors awaited a Tuesday congressional hearing where U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke is expected to give signals regarding the direction of U.S. monetary policy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.0351 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, equal to Friday's close.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If Mr. Bernanke gives signals Tuesday that he is preparing a fresh round of quantitative easing, the real would likely gain against the dollar, reflecting both increased optimism over the world economy and a depreciating dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The gains, though, would likely be modest, as in recent weeks the Brazilian government has suggested it will closely manage the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With industrial production contracting 4.3% in the 12 months to May, the Brazilian government is committed to preventing any appreciation of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a move meant to boost the competitiveness of Brazilian exports.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Comments by the Brazilian finance minister and the director of monetary policy at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in recent weeks hinted that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would sell reais or increase taxes on capital inflows in order to prevent the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from appreciating past BRL2.00 to the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, a ceiling seems to be established at BRL2.10 to the dollar, with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  selling dollar-swap contracts in recent weeks at times when the real was weakening sharply against the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A weaker real raises the prices of imports for Brazilian consumers.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The result of these government measures has been a stable exchange rate.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Today, we have an unofficial floor of BRL2.00 to the dollar and a ceiling of BRL2.10 to the dollar," said Joao Medeiros, a partner at Pioneer brokerage in Sao Paulo. "Internationally, we're just seeing more of the same, and the market is unmoved."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Most traders agree the real will stay in the narrow band established recently.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  made it clear it doesn't want the real stronger than BRL2.00 to the dollar," said Marcos Trabbold, chief of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at BT Associates brokerage in Sao Paulo. "For it to strengthen past BRL2.00 to the dollar, the government would have to alter the tax regime on capital inflows."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Brazilian government maintains a slew of taxes on capital inflows and transactions, intensified earlier this year when the real was trading at BRL1.70 to the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Brian Asher at brian.asher@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribe to WSJ: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires}}}\uc2 \f2  [ 16-07-12 2005GMT ]\f28 