\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Slightly Weaker Ahead of  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Decision\b0\par\par\uc2 531 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2012\par 21:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Brazil real trades in narrow band as market settles\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected to cut base rate Wednesday\par \par \uc2 --Real exits active trading at BRL2.0374 to the dollar\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   By Brian Asher \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RIO DE JANEIRO--The Brazilian real was slightly weaker in Tuesday trading, as investors awaited a rate cut expected Wednesday and digested a mixed bag of international and domestic economic data.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.0374 to the dollar according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, weaker than Monday's close at BRL2.0313 to the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Volatility was low, with the real staying close to BRL2.03 to the dollar throughout the day.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Many traders now expect the real to remain in a narrow band, as the Brazilian government appears to be targeting an exchange rate between BRL2.00 and BRL2.10 to the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In recent weeks, when the real has weakened sharply against the dollar, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prevent further depreciation of the real, selling dollar-swap contracts.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In addition, both the finance minister and a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official made comments last week suggesting the government will prevent the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from appreciating past BRL2.00 to the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazilian industry declined 4.3% in the 12 months to May, and President Dilma Rousseff's government seems determined to boost the competitiveness of Brazilian exports through a weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Market watchers expect the Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monetary policy committee to announce a half-point cut to the country's Selic base rate on Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Such a cut would bring the Selic base rate to a historic low of 8.0%, putting pressure on the real to depreciate, but the cut has been expected for some time, meaning only a surprise decision to make a deeper cut or hold rates steady would strongly affect the real.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Also pressuring the real has been the dwindling growth prospects for Brazil's economy, where economists now expect growth of only 2% this year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Business confidence in Brazil has been hurt by the euro-zone crisis, and European leaders Tuesday extended the deadline for Spain's budget cuts, but moved no closer to a European banking union.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The euro weakened slightly, which could have helped the real weaken against the dollar here as well," said Luiz Carlos Arenelle, a trader a Dascam brokerage in Sao Paulo.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 However, to Brazil's economy, Europe is of less concern than China, Brazil's largest trading partner.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Data released in China Tuesday was ambiguous, as exports were strong but imports disappointed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The mixed data and expectations of exchange-rate targeting combined to produce a trading session with very little volatility.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The market was very calm," said Luiz Carlos Baldan, director of Fourtrade brokerage in Sao Paulo. "The real weakened slightly on the expectation of the Selic base rate cut, but nothing unexpected happened and nothing expected didn't happen, so we didn't see any big movements."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tomorrow, all eyes will be on Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as it announces its much-anticipated monetary policy decision.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Write to Brian Asher at brian.asher@dowjones.com [ 10-07-12 1945GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120710e87a0017v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
