\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Closes Little Changed, Gains Seen in Medium Term\b0\par\par\uc2 517 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 2012\par 21:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --The real exited active trading at BRL2.0248 to the dollar compared with Wednesday's close at BRL2.0260\par \par \uc2 --Movements are due to external events\par \par \uc2 --Real expected to gain against the dollar in coming weeks if outlook in Europe improves\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Jeffrey T. Lewis \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BRASILIA--The Brazilian real closed little changed against the dollar Thursday, after multiple ups and downs, with traders and analysts expecting it to gain against the greenback in the coming weeks as Europe takes more measures to resolve its sovereign debt and bank crises.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.0248 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, compared with Wednesday's close at BRL2.0260.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthened in early trading after the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut its benchmark interest rate. The real reversed course and weakened at midday, then regained some of its earlier advance in late trading before closing the day nearly unchanged.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ECB's move was welcome, as it should boost Europe's sluggish economy, and the improving outlook for the region's problems should help the real strengthen in coming weeks, said Clodoir Vieira, an economist at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Souza Barros\f28 \uc2 \f2  brokerage in Sao Paulo.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The real should strengthen a bit against the dollar, because if Europe comes to an agreement, then other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should be more stable," Vieira said. "The movement we're seeing here with the real is mostly because of external factors. Positive events in Europe will cause the dollar to weaken."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ECB cut its benchmark rate Thursday to a record low of 0.75%, from 1.0%. The bank also cut its overnight deposit and lending rates by 0.25 percentage point each, to 0% and 1.50% respectively. Cutting the deposit rate is expected to encourage banks to lend out excess funds overnight instead of depositing them at the ECB.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real is generally trending stronger against the dollar, and only \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and comments from the Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Brazilian politicians are helping to keep the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around the level of two or more to the dollar, said Riberto Frederico, a trader at the OM brokerage in Sao Paulo.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I think the real should return to BRL1.95 more or less, around there, but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the government have made it clear they don't want that," Frederico said.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  repeatedly in recent months, at times to weaken the real, though at other times to strengthen it. Brazilian President Dilma Rousseff and Finance Minister Guido Mantega have also acted on multiple occasions to weaken the real in order to make the country's exports more competitive.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Earlier in the day, two more of the world's most important central banks moved to ease policy, with the Bank of England increasing its asset purchase program by 50 billion pounds to GBP325 billion, and the People's Bank of China cutting its benchmark interest rates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Write to Jeffrey T. Lewis at jeffrey.lewis@dowjones.com [ 05-07-12 1959GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120705e8750010b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
