\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2 : Would Resume Dollar Buys Via Futures - Report\b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2012\par 19:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA--Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would resume dollar buying if necessary in the futures market before considering a return to spot market purchases, Monetary Policy Director Aldo Mendes said Tuesday, according to the Estado news agency.\par \par \uc2 "The dynamics (of the exchange market) have been concentrated in the futures segment," he said. "If we had to resume \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it would be in futures."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, has strengthened against the dollar in recent sessions after weakening sharply in the first months of this year in response to global market turbulence and investor risk aversion.\par \par \uc2 Because of the weakening, the bank earlier this year suspended long-running spot market purchases aimed at curbing volatility and building the country's foreign reserves.\par \par \uc2 To prevent excess weakening in recent weeks, the bank sold swap contracts that allowed investors to exchange paper indexed to domestic interest rates for bonds linked to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 While he didn't rule out further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on either the buying or selling end, Mr. Mendes noted that the tendency of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had reversed toward strengthening with improving sentiment brought by Europe's recent decision to support banks in that region.\par \par \uc2 "There's a better perception in relation to external risk," he said. "In a general manner, the announcement following the meeting (of EU leaders) brought some relief for risk appetite."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  director said the institution didn't have a specific target level for \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  only according to market liquidity needs. However, he said he believed that a real stronger than BRL2.00 to the dollar would have negative effects on local industry.\par \par \uc2 "Industry has been weak," he said. "In a certain manner, this increases the possibility that the government might want to see the dollar at a stronger level than it is today."\par \par \uc2 Brazil's IBGE institute Tuesday reported that the country's industrial production fell 0.9% in May from April. The result represented a third consecutive monthly decline.\par \par \uc2 Write to Gerald Jeffris at gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 -0- [ 07-03-12 1320ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020120703e8730006p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
