\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Brazilian Real Likely to Extend Weakness -\uc2 Credit Agricole\b0\par\par\uc2 149 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2012\par 18:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 12:40 EDT - "We view the Brazilian real as overvalued in general," says Sireen Harajli of \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2 . Brazil's government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  passed various measures to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, and she expects the dollar to remain between BRL1.9 and BRL2.10. In recent months, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the dollar rises above BRL2.10. Still, the real is expected to weaken gradually as concerns about slowing growth in Brazil and its trading partner China, and less domestic consumption, are weighing on investors. The dollar is trading at BRL1.9953, up 0.5% on the day, after closing sharply lower Monday at BRL1.9858. (prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Call us at (212) 416-3100 or email bradley.davis@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 [ 03-07-12 1640GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1085   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120703e873000y2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
