\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Brazil Real Strengthens Past BRL2 Against Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 539 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 2012\par 22:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--The Brazilian real gained Monday to the strongest level in more than a month on continued optimism following last week's European summit, and as the prospect of continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen the real offset concerns about sluggish growth at home and abroad.\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading at BRL1.9874 to the dollar, stronger than its previous close at BRL2.0104, and the first time it closed stronger than BRL2 versus the dollar since May, according to Tullett Prebon via Factset.\par \par \uc2 European markets were broadly higher Monday as the optimism generated by last week's summit of European Union leaders carried over to the start of the second half of the year. The hopeful outlook helped investors to look past some weak economic data, which showed activity at euro-zone factories continue to fall sharply in June, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  area's unemployment rate rose to a fresh record high in May.\par \par \uc2 "Everyone was saying that Spain and Italy were next to fall, but Germany and France decided to help inject liquidity so that what happened to Greece wouldn't happen to them," said Celso Siqueira, fixed-income manager at Sao Paulo brokerage Advanced Corretora.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, meanwhile, economists once again reduced their estimates for Brazil growth this year, according to a weekly \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  survey published Monday. Economists expect gross domestic product to expand 2.05% this year, down from 2.18% estimated in the previous survey. Inflation expectations also fell, to 4.93% from 4.95%, reaffirming the view that Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has room to cut rates and stimulate growth as inflation heads toward its target of 4.5%.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began cutting rates in August, when the benchmark Selic stood at 12.5%, and it is widely expected to cut the rate by half a point next week to 8%. Economists surveyed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expect the Selic to end this year at 7.5%.\par \par \uc2 Falling rates reduce the appeal of Brazil, which in the past attracted heavy inflows as investors borrowed at near-zero rates abroad to snap up higher-yielding Brazilian assets.\par \par \uc2 To counter the weakening of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been stepping up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, holding auctions to put more dollars in the market. Last week, the bank held three swap auctions, selling the equivalent of $9 billion in contracts.\par \par \uc2 Although $3 billion of those were to replace expiring contracts, the rest was new money, serving as "a clear signal" to some analysts that the government will prevent any weakening of the real beyond the level of BRL2.10 to the dollar, which it touched last week.\par \par \uc2 "The previous time we hit BRL2.10 per dollar, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  carried out $16 billion in auctions, and the real climbed back to less than BRL2 per dollar," Mr. Siqueira said in a phone interview. "Last week, they carried out several auctions, injecting almost $10 billion in the swap markets, and that was reflected in the market."\par \par \uc2 Write to Paulo Winterstein at paulo.winterstein@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 02, 2012 16:27 ET (20:27 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120702e872006i4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
