\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil real gains past 2/dlr, Mexico gains\b0\par\par\uc2 481 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 2012\par 17:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Brazil real gains on expectation of more cenbank action\par \par \uc2 * US data, fading Pena Nieto optimism weigh on Mexican peso\par \par \uc2 By Natalia Cacioli and Rachel Uranga\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO/MEXICO CITY, July 2 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real on Monday dropped below 2 per dollar for the first time in over a month on rising expectations of additional \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the peso edged up after presidential elections.\par \par \uc2 The real gained 1.13 percent to 1.9865 per dollar as investors took \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week as a sign policymakers will not allow the exchange rate to depreciate much further.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's actions last week made it clear it doesn't like the real above 2 per dollar," said Darwin Dib, chief economist at CM Capital Markets.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week eased rules on export prepayment and sold 180,000 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps worth $9 billion in three auctions. While the first measure allows more dollars to flow into the country, the swap auction boosts the supply of greenbacks in the futures market.\par \par \uc2 In Mexico, the peso edged up 0.15 percent after presidential front runner Enrique Pena Nieto claimed a narrower victory than expected in Sunday's elections. Analysts said the lower level of support meant optimism about reforms he has promised could soon vanish.\par \par \uc2 Still, Pena Nieto vowed on Monday to focus his energies on energy, labor and tax reforms and said he was willing to strike deals with opponents to get his efforts passed before taking office in December.\par \par \uc2 "There was an expectation that not only would Pena Nieto win but in his ability to pass a very aggressive reform package," said Maya Hernandez, a Latin American strategist at \uc2 HSBC\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 The president-elect's victory margin was smaller than expected and federal election results suggested his Institutional Revolutionary Party and its allies would struggle to win a majority in congress, complicating reform efforts.\par \par \uc2 "The first take impression is that he's not going to come in with an overwhelming majority in congress necessary to pass these reforms," Hernandez said.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the session the peso slipped after data showed the U.S. manufacturing sector unexpectedly contracted in June, weighing on prospects for the Mexican economy. The United States accounts for most of Mexico's exports.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices from Reuters at 20:30 GMT:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                 daily %  year-to\par                                   change   date %\par                          Latest            change\par  Brazil real             1.9865     1.13    -5.94\par                                           \par  Mexico peso            13.3350     0.15     4.76\par                                           \par   Argentina peso*        5.9400     0.17   -20.37\par                                           \par    Chile peso                    National holiday\par                     \par      Colombia peso               National holiday\par                     \par    Peru sol              2.6520     0.45     1.70\par                                           \par * Argentine peso's rate between                  \par                      brokerages           \par                                          