\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Weakens Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 522 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2012\par 21:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -European debt crisis weighs on emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold dollar-swap auction Wednesday\par \par \uc2 -Brazil real exits active trading at BRL2.0701 to the dollar\par \par \uc2 By Brian Asher\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO--The Brazilian real weakened against the dollar Tuesday, as investors bought up greenbacks on expectations of prolonged turmoil in the euro zone and weak economic growth in Brazil.\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.0701 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, weaker than Monday's close at BRL2.0654 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday's depreciation of the real came in spite of a morning announcement that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would auction 60,000 dollar-swap contracts Wednesday. The swaps on offer are worth a total of $3 billion.\par \par \uc2 The move was unusual in that past \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have seen the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announce auctions to be held the same day.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was strange. I can't remember the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  like this. Normally, if it announces a swap auction for the following day, it's at the end of the afternoon," said Ovidio Soares, a trader at the Interbolsa brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 Dollar-swap auctions allow investors to exchange paper linked to domestic interest rates for contracts indexed to the U.S. dollar. The auctions are a tool to smooth volatility in the exchange market at times when the Brazilian real is weakening sharply against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Wednesday's auction will be the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first dollar swap contract auction since June 11.\par \par \uc2 The real strengthened slightly in afternoon trading after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's statement, but not enough to gain back morning losses.\par \par \uc2 The perception that the euro-zone crisis is nowhere near its conclusion has battered emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week, as investors assume the European summit on Thursday and Friday will produce little in the way of concrete results.\par \par \uc2 A report Tuesday that German Chancellor Angela Merkel had already ruled out the possibility of shared European debt reinforced the low expectations ahead of the summit.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, too, investors found causes for concern.\par \par \uc2 Sluggish economic growth shows no signs of picking up, and economists are now predicting an expansion of just 2.18% in Brazil's gross domestic product this year.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday, the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  released data that showed non-performing loans had increased yet again in May, stoking fears of a bursting consumer credit bubble in Latin America's largest economy.\par \par \uc2 "The announcement of the swap auction for tomorrow calmed the market a little bit, but overall current economic conditions are going to continue to pressure the real to weaken," said Reginaldo Siaca, manager of the Advanced brokerage in Sao Paulo. "The downgrade of Spain's banks, stagnation in the U.S., and lower than expected growth in China and Brazil have made investors want to protect themselves with dollars."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Siaca added that he expects the real to stay between BRL2.05 and BRL2.10 to the dollar in the near term.\par \par \uc2 