\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  fall on euro zone uncertainty\b0\par\par\uc2 538 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 2012\par 17:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds details)\par \par \uc2 * Investors worry EU summit will fail to solve debt crisis\par \par \uc2 * Expectations of cenbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  support \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  real\par \par \uc2 * Real closes flat, Mexican peso falls 0.5 pct\par \par \uc2 By Natalia Cacioli\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, June 25 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened on Monday on fear that a summit of European leaders later this week would do little to stop the euro-zone debt crisis from spreading further and weighing on world economic prospects.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso lost 0.5 percent while the Chilean peso slumped 1.2 percent as investors pulled money from emerging-market assets and rushed to the perceived safety of the dollar, which gained around 0.4 percent against the euro.\par \par \uc2 In a sign of investors' growing aversion to risk, yield spreads between emerging market government bonds and U.S. Treasuries widened 7 basis points to 378 basis points, according to \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2 's EMBI+ index. The index is on track for its largest one-day spike since the beginning of the month.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real was an exception, however. It traded lower during most of the session but closed practically flat as investors feared the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "World stocks are falling and the euro is weakening sharply, but the real is not reflecting those moves because investors believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Italo dos Santos, a manager at the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  desk of Icap brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with the sale of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps since June 11, but the mere possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action has helped curb the real's depreciation.\par \par \uc2 The real has weakened 2.2 percent so far in June, and remains about 9.4 percent down since the beginning of the year.\par \par \uc2 RISING EURO UNCERTAINTY\par \par \uc2 Uncertainty related to the euro zone is poised to rise this week, before European leaders meet in Brussels on Thursday and Friday, in a bid to put an end to the crisis which on Monday forced Spain to request a package worth up to 100 billion euros to rescue its banks.\par \par \uc2 But hopes of faster fiscal integration in the euro zone, the solution many investors would like to see, are fading as German Chancellor Angela Merkel repeats her opposition to shared liability for the region's debts.\par \par \uc2 "Markets remain very pessimistic and uncomfortable," said Silvio Campos Neto, an economist with Tendencias consultancy in Sao Paulo. "Investors are speculating that nothing will be decided at the EU summit this week."\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices from Reuters at 21:20 GMT:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                             daily %  year-to-d\par                                      change       te %\par                            Latest               change\par Brazil real                  2.0660      0.06      -9.56\par                                            