\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Opens Weaker on U.S. Growth Concerns\b0\par\par\uc2 486 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2012\par 14:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Investors continue to search for dollars amid global uncertainty\par \par \uc2 --U.S. data disappoints, adds to fears out of euro zone, China\par \par \uc2 --Real trading at BRL2.0566 to the dollar as of 1215 GMT\par \par \uc2 By Brian Asher\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO--The Brazilian real traded weaker Friday morning as investors continued to move cautiously after disappointing data Thursday revealed weakness in the U.S. economy.\par \par \uc2 The real was trading at BRL2.0566 to the dollar at 1215 GMT, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, weaker than Thursday's close at BRL2.0530 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have mostly tracked news out of the euro zone recently, with investors rushing to dollars on bad news out of Europe and buying back emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when fears recede.\par \par \uc2 But this week, the focus has been squarely on the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Disappointing data released in the U.S. Thursday caused equity markets and emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  everywhere to tumble as housing data and jobless claims suggested the U.S. economy is slowing. This data came on the heels of a U.S. Federal Reserve announcement Wednesday that it had revised down its projections for 2012 economic growth.\par \par \uc2 But despite the gloomy economic outlook, the U.S. Federal Reserve did not choose to aggressively expand its monetary stimulus programs Wednesday, leading some investors to believe the Fed is running out of ammunition in the face of a deteriorating global economic situation.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile China, Brazil's largest trading partner and a driver of world commodity prices, continues to see slower economic growth. The HSBC China manufacturing purchasing managers' index, or PMI, released Thursday showed that in June China's manufacturing sector had contracted for an eighth consecutive month.\par \par \uc2 With no major data releases expected Friday, traders will be watching equity markets and bracing for any news out of the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 Some traders expect \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if the real weakens past BRL2.08 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts in order to control volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and stem the depreciation of the real. Dollar-swap auctions allow investors to exchange paper linked to domestic interest rates for contracts indexed to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The real has depreciated this year from BRL1.70 to the dollar in February to its current level close to BRL2.05 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Contributing to the real's depreciation has been a campaign by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to aggressively cut the country's Selic base interest rate, now at a historic low of 8.5%. Data released Thursday in Brazil showed inflation decelerating, reinforcing expectations of further rate cuts this year and adding pressure on the real to weaken.\par \par \uc2 Write to Brian Asher at brian.asher@dowjones.com [ 22-06-12 1255GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120622e86m000py\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
