\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Opens Stronger As Investors Eye Risks Ahead\b0\par\par\uc2 By Matthew Cowley   \par \uc2 362 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 2012\par 14:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened on Tuesday morning, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  played some catch-up after lagging its peers on Monday, but there were plenty of obstacles ahead to keep investors' attention.\par \par \uc2 The real hadn't kept up with the rally in other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, in the wake of the Greek election, but it was the strongest gainer among Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  early on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 At 1244 GMT, the dollar was trading at BRL2.0505, weaker than BRL2.0608 late Monday, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 Concerns across the euro-zone were mixed, with Greek politicians appearing to be moving towards an agreement over forming a coalition, following Sunday's election result. But the Spanish government was forced to pay an expensive price to sell debt, while in Germany, the widely-watched ZEW economic expectations index fell to -16.9 in June from May's unrevised 10.8.\par \par \uc2 The dollar, meanwhile, was weaker amid some speculation that the U.S. Federal Reserve may on Wednesday unveil more monetary policy easing to combat the ongoing economic weakness.\par \par \uc2 Traders in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  are also still awaiting further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , should the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  start to lose ground rapidly. Strategists at Citi pointed to the tame inflation data in Brazil, which shows prices converging on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target, so "we may infer that government is not as worried regarding the current \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  level as it was two weeks ago."\par \par \uc2 Earlier Tuesday, the private-sector Getulio Vargas Foundation said its general price index, known as the IGP-M, picked up 0.63% between May 21 and June 10, compared with a 1% rise between April 21 and May 10.\par \par \uc2 The latest figure was in line with analysts' expectations for an increase of between 0.50% and 0.75%; wholesale and construction costs were the main drivers, while consumer prices were almost unchanged.\par \par \uc2 The rolling IGP-M rate for the 12 months through June 10 was 5.11%.\par \par \uc2 Write to Matthew Cowley at matthew.cowley@dowjones.com [ 19-06-12 1250GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120619e86j000pt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
