\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Closes Stronger as European Tensions Ease\b0\par\par\uc2 543 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 2012\par 22:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Real closes stronger on Greek elections, Spanish bond sale\par \par \uc2 --U.S. Fed expected to further ease monetary policy Wednesday\par \par \uc2 --Real exits active trading at BRL2.030 to the dollar\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Brian Asher \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RIO DE JANEIRO--The Brazilian real strengthened against the dollar Tuesday as tensions in Europe's periphery economies eased slightly and investors expected U.S. officials to announce another round of monetary stimulus on Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.0300 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, stronger than Monday's close at BRL2.0608 to the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil belatedly joined an emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rally that began Monday after Greek voters elected a pro-euro government in parliamentary elections Sunday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In other news out of Europe, Spain's bond auction was slightly less painful than expected, with yields on 12-month government bonds weighing in at 5.07%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Midday rumors of a move by the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to buy bonds from Europe's periphery economies proved to be unsubstantiated, and the woes in Europe's less competitive economies are certainly not over. European leaders at the Group of 20 summit in Mexico did, however, express support for a European banking union with the power to regulate banks and secure deposits.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Also boosting the real was the expectation that the U.S. Federal Reserve will unveil further monetary stimulus measures Wednesday to bolster a sluggish economic recovery in the U.S.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. May housing data released Tuesday were mixed, with new housing starts falling short of expectations while new housing licenses reached their highest level since 2008.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tuesday's gains bucked a recent weakening trend for the real, as investors have fled to dollars amid uncertainty over the European sovereign debt crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Before recent losses, Brazilian exporters had struggled with an overvalued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , with the real this year trading as high as BRL1.7 to the greenback in February before falling to its current band between BRL2.00 and BRL2.05 to the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After complaining of an overvalued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earlier this year, Brazilian policymakers now seem uncomfortable with the real's rapid depreciation.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in recent weeks, selling swaps to inject dollars into the market and stem the weakening of the real. But the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has not entered the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market since last week, and some analysts now say the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's main goal is not to peg the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to the dollar but to prevent exchange-rate volatility.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "With regards to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has in general shown that it doesn't have a target for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," Arminio Fraga, a former president of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said at an event. "It doesn't like turbulence. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  doesn't want a mini panic such as the one in 2008. I continue to think that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  doesn't have a target for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, all eyes on Wednesday will be on the statement coming out of the U.S. Federal Reserve as investors hope for more monetary stimulus in the world's largest economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Brian Asher at brian.asher@dowjones.com [ 19-06-12 2042GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120619e86j000zx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
