\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Closes Stronger vs. Dollar After Volatile Session\b0\par\par\uc2 366 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 2012\par 22:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--The Brazilian real enjoyed a bumpy ride Thursday, but ended the day slightly stronger against the dollar, as investors braced for this weekend's Greek elections, which may determine the future course of the euro-zone crisis.\par \par \uc2 "Investors are seeking dollars as a protective measure ahead of the Greek elections on Sunday," said Jose Carlos Amado, a trader at Sao Paulo's Renascenca brokerage. "Volatility should continue Friday. It could ease next week if it looks like Greece is going to stay in the euro zone."\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.0545 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet. This was stronger than the late-morning trough of BRL2.0790 for the real, and against Thursday's open of BRL2.0637.\par \par \uc2 Traders said volatility increased in late-morning trading following a news conference by Finance Minister Guido Mantega in Brasilia. Mantega warned that the days of easy international financial-market liquidity are over.\par \par \uc2 Mantega was commenting on a government move, earlier Thursday, removing a 6.0% financial \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  tax on overseas loans with terms of between two years and five years.\par \par \uc2 By opening the door to more foreign loans, Brazil's government is seeking to increase dollar flows into the country, analysts said. However, the measure may be a case of too little, too late.\par \par \uc2 Andre Perfeito, chief economist at Sao Paulo's Gradual brokerage, said, "Removing the tax at this point doesn't help now that global investors are fleeing to liquidity."\par \par \uc2 Said Amado: "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to continue its recent policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever there is an increase in volatility." However, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Thursday.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have come in the form of auctions of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts. The contracts offer investors the opportunity to exchange bonds linked to interest rates for paper indexed to the U.S. dollar. The auctions tend to support the real against the dollar by giving investors an additional dollar-hedging tool.\par \par \uc2 --Paulo Winterstein contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Tom Murphy at tom.murphy@dowjones.com [ 14-06-12 2023GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120614e86e0013k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
