\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Opens Weaker Amid European Malaise:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Possible\b0\par\par\uc2 368 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2012\par 15:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real weakened in early trading Tuesday as global risk appetite remains subdued amid concerns over the efficacy of European efforts to solve the regional debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 Traders indicated further action by Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may occur to stem the real's weakening.\par \par \uc2 The real traded at BRL2.0533 to the U.S. dollar recently, weaker than its exit from active trading Monday at BRL2.0468, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  thus surpassed the BRL2.05 barrier that traders believe may spark new action by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  with three swap auctions to curb trading volatility so far this month.\par \par \uc2 In global markets, investors reportedly continued with uncertainty over the efficacy of bailout plans for Spanish banks announced at the weekend. The euro fell in value against the dollar in trading earlier in the day, after ratings firm Fitch on Monday downgraded the credit ratings of Spain's biggest banks, Santander and \uc2 BBVA\uc2 . Sterling also took a hit after the U.K. announced industrial production remained stable at weak levels in April.\par \par \uc2 Traders' attention turned to Italy, which is plagued by low growth and high-cost zones. Italy is expected to be the next euro-zone country to need an international bailout package. Share prices of Italian banks fell in local trading.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, Monday's "disappointing" economic data, with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts revising downward their GDP growth forecasts from a week ago, mean that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be "making sure it remains present in the market in order to stem \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness," the \uc2 Royal Bank of Scotland\uc2  said in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 "Though price weakness has been predominately on the back of flows, we cannot ignore continued disappointment in regards to economic data," RBS said. "According to the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weekly forecast of private sector estimates, GDP growth forecasts for 2012 were revised lower for the fifth consecutive week and are now at 2.53%, down from 3.20% four weeks ago and 4.5% since early 2011."\par \par \uc2 Write to diana.kinch@dowjones.com [ 12-06-12 1323GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120612e86c000t6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
