\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Closes Sharply Weaker Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 665 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2012\par 21:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real weakens despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction of dollar swaps\par \par \uc2 --Trade deficit, downward pressure on real offset Spain bank bailout\par \par \uc2 --Brazilian real exits active trading at BRL2.0468 to the dollar\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Jeff Fick \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil's real \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  closed sharply weaker against the U.S. dollar Monday, despite a Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar-swap auction and early-session euphoria over a deal to bail out Spain's troubled banking sector.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.0468 to the dollar, well off Friday's closing quote of BRL2.0248, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , however, failed to break the BRL2.05 barrier that the market believes is the Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's de facto ceiling for the real, with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hitting a session weakest at BRL2.0495 to the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The market opened with the real a bit stronger, but from there we saw strong pressure for the weakening of the real," said Pedro Zotovici, a trader at Sao Paulo's Multi Money brokerage.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had opened the session stronger, as investors cheered the weekend deal to recapitalize Spain's banking sector, which has been weighed down by bad loans doled out during the country's real-estate boom. The European Union will loan Spain up to $125 billion, with the final tally set to be disclosed by independent auditors later this month.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite the deal to rescue Spain's banks, investors still question whether the move will be enough to resolve the sector's troubles. In addition, the market is still nervous ahead of Sunday's elections in Greece. While the chances of a sudden Greek pullout from the euro zone have diminished, Greeks have reacted negatively to harsh austerity measures imposed as part of the country's rescue package and could opt to vote in politicians less willing to support the fiscal cuts.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real weakened past the BRL2.03 mark in a swift reversal during mid-morning trade, luring the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the sidelines with a dollar-swap auction. But the auction was far from a success, with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  selling $400 million worth of the $1 billion dollar-swap contracts it was prepared to sell. The real initially gained some ground against the dollar before falling back once again and weakening past the BRL2.04 mark.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The market did not like the terms set by the Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the auction, Mr. Zotovici said. "The bank is going to need to lower the price of the dollar in its swaps if it wants to continue \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar-swap auctions allow investors to exchange paper linked to domestic interest rates for contracts indexed to the U.S. dollar. The auctions are a tool to smooth volatility in the exchange market at times when the Brazilian real is weakening sharply against the dollar. Last week, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold a total of $2.02 billion in dollar swaps in two separate auctions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real also was undermined by Brazil's surprise trade deficit to kick off June, with the country registering a deficit of $325 million in the first 10 days of the month. The latest data made traders "nervous" and set off a search for dollars, Mr. Zotovici said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But some traders said there weren't any fundamental reasons for the real to weaken so sharply.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "You're not seeing the stock market falling drastically. No one is desperately seeking dollars," said Olvidio Soares, a trader at Interbolsa. "What we see in the market right now is pure speculation that is causing this pronounced volatility."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Soares called the real's downturn "unjustified" and said the low volume of dollar swaps offered by the Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  showed "there is no real rush for dollars."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Brian Asher in Rio de Janeiro contributed to this article.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Jeff Fick at Jeff.Fick@dowjones.com. [ 11-06-12 2013GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120611e86b000zj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
