\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Opens Stronger After Spain Requests Bank Bailout\b0\par\par\uc2 611 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2012\par 14:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Brazil's real opens stronger as Spanish bank bailout eases tensions in global markets\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players expected to remain cautious ahead of Greek elections Sunday\par \par \uc2 --Brazilian real opens trading at BRL2.0197, stronger from Friday's close at BRL2.0248\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Jeff Fick \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Brazilian real traded stronger at the open Monday as a European Union deal to bail out Spain's troubled banking sector boosted morale, although gains may be short-lived ahead of next weekend's elections in debt-saddled Greece.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil's real joined other global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , especially the euro, in gaining ground against the U.S. dollar as the deal with Spain boosted investor sentiment. The Brazilian real opened at BRL2.0197 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet. That was stronger from Friday's close at BRL2.0248.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Global markets cheered the weekend deal to recapitalize Spain's banking sector, which has been weighed down by bad loans doled out during the country's real-estate boom. The European Union will loan Spain up to $125 billion, with the final tally set to be disclosed by independent auditors later this month. The deal eliminates, for the moment, a key pressure point in the ongoing European financial crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The recapitalization plan should help reduce "market anxiety about how [Spain] will return to building its path out of the crisis," said Miriam Tavares, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  director at Sao Paulo-based trading house AGK Corretora.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Looming on the horizon, however, are elections in Greece. While the chances of a sudden Greek pullout of the euro zone have diminished, the Greek people have reacted negatively to harsh austerity measures imposed as part of the country's rescue package and could opt to vote in politicians less willing to support the fiscal cuts.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Market watchers also reacted positively to economic indicators released over the weekend in China, a key market for Brazilian exporters. The country's trade surplus advanced and inflation decelerated in May, while industrial production topped April numbers despite coming in lower than expected. The figures showed that while China's economy should pick up in coming months, officials still have room to adopt additional stimulus measures after the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last week made its first interest-rate cut in three years.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the market is watching carefully for further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after two dollar-swap auctions last week. The bank sold about $2.02 billion in dollar swaps last week at two separate auctions after the real weakened to near the BRL2.05 mark.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar-swap auctions allow investors to exchange paper linked to domestic interest rates for contracts indexed to the U.S. dollar. The auctions are a tool to smooth volatility in the exchange market at times when the Brazilian real is weakening sharply against the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves suggest that levels above BRL2.05 will draw \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with swaps, signaling that the [\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate] between BRL2.0 and BRL2.05 is likeliest at this time," Ms. Tavares of AGK Corretora said in her morning note to clients.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Economists and market analysts also continue to cut their outlook for growth in Latin America's largest economy, according to the latest weekly market survey released by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Monday. The survey estimate for Brazil's 2012 gross-domestic-product growth is now 2.53%, down from 2.72% last week. That was the fifth-consecutive reduction to the forecast. The outlook for 2013 also was cut, to 4.30% from 4.50%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Write to Jeff Fick at Jeff.Fick@dowjones.com [ 11-06-12 1236GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120611e86b000sc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
