\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Mexico peso up on cenbank statement; real trims loss\b0\par\par\uc2 810 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 2012\par 15:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Mexico peso gaining after cenbank statement)\par \par \uc2 * Mexico peso gains as cenbank dashes rate cut speculation\par \par \uc2 * Brazil cenbank says global downturn sapping inflation\par \par \uc2 * Chile's peso falls with copper prices, muted inflation\par \par \uc2 * Brazil real 0.1 pct lower, Mexico peso up 0.7 pct\par \par \uc2 By Walter Brandimarte\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, June 8 (Reuters) - Mexico's peso strengthened on Friday as policymakers dashed speculation of imminent rate cuts in the country, while the Brazilian real trimmed early losses after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Other Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained weaker, however, as investors worried about the global economic impact of an escalating European debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso traded lower early in the session but bounced after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its key interest rate unchanged at 4.5 percent. The bank made clear its next move could go either way, dropping a flirtation with a rate cut that had weighed on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bank also acknowledged a "moderate" risk to inflation from a weaker peso, which has lost about 10 percent since mid March.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso was 0.7 percent stronger in the afternoon, at 13.9699 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real also opened lower but trimmed losses after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with a sale of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, which essentially increase the supply of dollars in the market.\par \par \uc2 That was the second time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered to sell \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps this week. The auction was announced when the real traded slightly above 2.04 per dollar, reinforcing a market perception that, at least for now, policymakers are drawing an informal line around 2.05 per greenback.\par \par \uc2 "When the real reaches a certain level, of 2.05 per dollar, we know the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Jankiel Santos, chief economist with BES Investimento in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 The real was 0.13 percent weaker in the afternoon, at 2.0292 per greenback.\par \par \uc2 Other Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened, however, as investors cautiously watched political and economic developments in the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 Spain is expected to request European aid for its struggling banks over the weekend, becoming the fourth and biggest European country to seek assistance since the euro zone's debt crisis began.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso lost 0.12 percent as prices of copper , the country's main export product, fell to a six-month low in London.\par \par \uc2 "Markets are all in the red, with stocks falling, copper prices tumbling and the dollar strengthening against the euro - all those factors are negative for the peso," said a trader in Santiago.\par \par \uc2 Chile's lower-than-expected inflation reading for May also contributed to a weaker peso as it eliminated any speculation of an immediate rate hike by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Chile's consumer price index was unchanged in May from the previous month, the government statistics agency INE said. Analysts polled by Reuters had forecast a median 0.2 percent increase for the index.\par \par \uc2 MORE RATE CUTS IN BRAZIL\par \par \uc2 Brazil's interest-rate futures slid on Friday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  suggested it is poised to keep cutting the country's base interest rate.\par \par \uc2 Interest-rate contracts maturing in January 2013 <0#2DIJ:> dropped 7 basis points to 7.820 percent after policymakers said in minutes of their latest monetary policy meeting that a global economic downturn is helping to bring inflation back to target.\par \par \uc2 The bank's committee, known as the Copom, repeated its guidance that more rate cuts should be conducted "sparingly." Policymakers unanimously cut the benchmark Selic rate for a seventh consecutive time to a record low of 8.5 percent on May 30.\par \par \uc2 "This leaves the door open for additional rate cuts," said Alberto Ramos, a senior economist with \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2 , adding that the next cuts should be "moderate," or smaller than 75 basis points, and "somewhat data dependent."\par \par \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  expects Brazil will cut the Selic again to 8.0 percent in July.\par \par \uc2 "An extension of the easing cycle beyond the July meeting is certainly possible particularly if the external backdrop continues to deteriorate and the domestic real business cycle dynamics remain sluggish," Ramos said.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices from Reuters at 1307 GMT:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                             daily %  yearly %\par                                      change    change\par                            Latest            \par Brazil real                  2.0292     -0.13     -7.92\par                                              \par Mexico peso                 13.9699      0.69      0.00\par                                              \par Argentina peso*              5.9300     -0.17    -20.24\par                                              \par Chile peso                 501.0000     -0.12      3.65\par                                              \par Colombia peso            1,777.5000     -0.33      9.05\par                                              \par Peru sol                     2.6820     -0.04      0.56\par                                              \par * Argentine peso's rate between                        \par brokerages                                     \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Froilan Romero in Santiago, Natalia Cacioli in Sao Paulo; Editing by Andrew Hay)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | U | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120611e868000rn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
