\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Closes Stronger On  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 641 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 2012\par 21:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real strengthens after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells $1.01 billion in dollar swaps\par \par \uc2 --European crisis, slowing global economy still key factor in trading\par \par \uc2 --Brazilian real exits active trading at BRL2.0248 to the dollar\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Jeff Fick \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil's real \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  shrugged off a gloomy global scenario and low post-holiday volume Friday to end stronger against the U.S. dollar, gaining ground on the greenback after the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surprised the market with a dollar-swap auction.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors returned from the mid-week Corpus Christi holiday that closed Brazilian financial markets Thursday in a sour mood, with the real trending weaker at the start of trading amid concerns about Europe's ongoing debt crisis and a slowing global economy. "The market today suffered from a lack of liquidity throughout the session," said Luiz Carlos Baldan, a director at Sao Paulo trading house Fourtrade. "With the external situation still difficult and no resolution in the European crisis, we expected the [stock market] to fall and the dollar to strengthen."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The market's mood was defensive on growing expectations for disappointing news about the global scenario, traders said. China's decision to lower interest rates Thursday raised alarm bells that the rate cut was a pre-emptive move ahead of disappointing economic indicators. Wholesale and consumer price inflation figures are among a slew of data expected to be released in China over the weekend.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Worries about Spain's banks also dragged down the euro after Fitch Ratings downgraded Spain's sovereign debt three notches to just above junk territory. Press reports raised the prospect that Spain could be ready to ask for international aid to prop up its struggling banking sector, perhaps as early as this weekend.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dour outlook pushed the real to a session-weakest BRL2.0411 to the dollar in late morning trade, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet. That drew the attention of the Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which jumped into the market with a surprise dollar-swap auction--the second such move this week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold $1.01 billion in dollar-swap contracts, two-thirds of the $1.5 billion the bank was prepared to sell as it moved to inject some dollar liquidity. The bank sold 20,400 contracts at two maturities, July 2 and Aug. 1. Dollar-swap auctions allow investors to exchange paper linked to domestic interest rates for contracts indexed to the U.S. dollar. The auctions are a tool to smooth volatility in the exchange market at times when the Brazilian real is weakening sharply against the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real immediately strengthened after the swap sale was announced, bouncing off session lows. The momentum held through the rest of the session, with the real exiting active trading at BRL2.0248 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet. That was stronger from Wednesday's close at BRL2.0298.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's latest moves have been designed to keep the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market on its toes, said Reginaldo Galhardo, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manager at Treviso.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at varying levels in the market for dollars," Mr. Galhardo said, noting recent dollar-swap auctions held at BRL2.08, BRL2.05 and BRL2.03. "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  doesn't want the market to know at what level it will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real has stabilized at slightly above the BRL2-to-the-dollar mark in recent weeks because that's what the market believes the government is targeting, Mr. Galhardo said. "The government wants the market to find an equilibrium that is good for everyone, not just one sector or the other," he added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Jeff Fick at jeff.fick@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Brian Asher in Rio de Janeiro contributed to this report. [ 08-06-12 1923GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120608e868001ad\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
