\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Slightly Stronger on Euro, Commodities\b0\par\par\uc2 492 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 2012\par 15:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Real opens at BRL2.0145/dlr Vs BRL2.0195/dlr Tuesday\par \par \uc2 --Stronger euro, higher commodities prices support real\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen "vigilant" against any volatility\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO --The Brazilian real strengthened slightly against the U.S. dollar in early trading Wednesday, as the euro gained against the greenback and global commodities prices advanced.\par \par \uc2 The real was trading at BRL2.0145 to the dollar early in the session, stronger against the Tuesday close of BRL2.0195, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 The euro strengthened against the dollar Wednesday after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held its base interest rate steady at 1.0%. Lower yields for Spanish and Italian debt also helped buoy the euro.\par \par \uc2 A stronger euro typically supports the real. Higher global prices for commodities also helped support the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar. Higher commodities prices bring more export revenue to Brazil.\par \par \uc2 Traders said market volume was thin Wednesday, ahead of a religious holiday Thursday that will keep Brazilian markets shuttered. Traders noted that many Brazilian businesses will remain closed Friday, with market volume likely to remain slim.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the real's strength could prove temporary, however.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian inflation figures, released earlier Wednesday, showed an unexpected decline in the 12-month inflation rate to 4.99% as of May from 5.10% as of April. The decline in inflation should encourage the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to speed up the tempo of interest rate cuts.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's Selic base interest rate is currently 8.5%. At its May meeting, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut the rate by a half percentage point. More rate cuts are likely in the coming months. With inflation in decline, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could cut the base rate to 7.5% or even lower, according to some economists.\par \par \uc2 But lower interest rates will tend to make Brazil a less attractive venue for foreign investors, leading to a long-term weakening of the Brazilian real against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Traders, however, noted that Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also been vigilant against any abrupt alteration in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  values.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has shown in recent days that even the slightest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can reverse the trend in trading," said Wanderlei Muniz, a trader at southern Brazil's Onnix brokerage.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks has limited its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sale of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts, rather than direct sale or purchase of dollars. Swap contracts allow investors to exchange paper indexed to interest rates for contracts linked to the U.S. dollar. The swaps offer investors a way to bolster their U.S. dollar hedging positions and typically strengthen the real against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 Muniz added, "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems comfortable with the real trading close to BRL2.00 to the dollar. Unless there is an abrupt departure from that baseline, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely."\par \par \uc2 Write to Tom Murphy at \b \highlight22\uc2 brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 @dowjones.com [ 06-06-12 1311GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120606e866000v1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
