\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real jumps 1 pct as  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 442 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2012\par 18:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  cenbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  when real weakened past 2.05\par \par \uc2 * G7 talks disappoint, driving Mexico peso down 0.3 pct\par \par \uc2 * Chile peso gains 0.5 pct on domestic growth data\par \par \uc2 By Walter Brandimarte\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, June 5 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real jumped more than 1 percent on Tuesday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed its market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a week hiatus, but the Mexican peso weakened after an emergency G7 conference call failed to allay euro zone concerns.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered to sell \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts early in the session when the real was practically unchanged from Monday's close of 2.0513 per dollar, reinforcing a market perception that policymakers were drawing a line around that level.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is reinforcing that ceiling," said Flavia Cattan-Naslausky, Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with RBS Securities. "The last time they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  was on May 25, when the real was trading around 2.03."\par \par \uc2 Brazilian government sources have told Reuters, however, that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not draw any hard lines in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market that it cannot defend in the event of a strong market shock.\par \par \uc2 The real jumped more than 1 percent right after the swap auction announcement. It added to gains later to trade around 2.0295 per dollar as data showed the U.S. services sector grew at a slightly faster pace in May.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. data came in above economists' expectations, offering a gleam of hope to markets that have been battered in the past few days by a series of disappointing economic data in the United States, China and Brazil.\par \par \uc2 Data showing Chile's economy was slowing down in line with market expectations also supported the Chilean peso, which rose about half a percentage point to 512.40 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "What is driving the peso is the domestic growth data," said Sergio Tricio, head of research at \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chile. "It shows the economy is solid, slowly decelerating as the rest of the world, but still attractive to foreign investors."\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, the Mexican peso lost 0.3 percent to 14.250 per U.S. dollar on concerns about an escalating European debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 Finance ministers of the Group of Seven industrialized countries held a conference call on Tuesday to discuss the euro zone but issued no statement after the talks, disappointing investors who expected a plan to deal with the crisis.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Natalia Cacioli in Sao Paulo and Moises Avila in Santiago; Editing by Andrea Ricci)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120608e8650013i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
