\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-EMERGING MARKETS-Mexico peso firms as vote fears ease, Brazil real dips\b0\par\par\uc2 532 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2012\par 00:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Refiles to additional subscribers)\par \par \uc2  * Mexico poll shows pro-market front runner holds big lead\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  real dips back to level that triggered \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  real dips 0.22 pct, Mexico peso firms 0.8 pct \par \par \uc2  By Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY, June 4 (Reuters) - Mexico's peso firmed on Monday, helped by a poll showing the pro-market frontrunner in the presidential race still had a healthy lead, while Brazil's real slipped back to a level that could trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  The peso received some support from a poll that showed Mexican opposition candidate Enrique Pena Nieto is still the frontrunner ahead of the July 1 presidential election, with a lead of nearly 14 percentage points. \par \par \uc2  The poll eased some investor nerves after a poll last week had shown leftist Andres Manuel Lopez Obrador had narrowed the gap to only four percentage points, stoking concerns that the race could be much closer than investors had been expecting.\par \par \uc2  "Investors had become concerned that (Lopez Obrador) could rise from the ashes to take the election," said Clyde Wardle, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 HSBC\uc2  in New York. "The more recent polls have taken away a little of those concerns that the market had."\par \par \uc2  Fund managers have been betting that a victory by Pena Nieto, from the opposition Institutional Revolutionary Party that ruled Mexico for most of the previous century, could unlock 15 years of stalled reforms and jump-start growth.\par \par \uc2  The Mexico peso  firmed 0.8 percent to 14.2080 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2  The peso may also have gotten some support from rising expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve could deliver more stimulus to support the economy of the United States, which buys nearly 80 percent of Mexican exports. \par \par \uc2  U.S. data on Monday showed orders for manufactured goods dropped 0.6 percent in April, its third decline in four months. That report followed Friday's jobs report that was much weaker than expected. \par \par \uc2  "There is some optimism because the bad data seen in the United States could be the incentive for additional stimulus from the Fed," said Mario Copca, an analyst at the CI brokerage.\par \par \uc2  Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also backed by gains in the euro on hopes Europe will use the euro zone's permanent bailout fund to rescue stricken banks. \par \par \uc2  Riskier assets, such as Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , often track the euro. Chile's peso firmed 0.6 percent to 515.20 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Fears that Europe's debt troubles could trigger another global financial crisis have driven Mexico's peso and Brazil real to three-year lows. Slumping growth in Brazil has also hurt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  there.\par \par \uc2  The Brazilian real , however, gave up early gains to bid down 0.22 percent at 2.0513 per dollar.\par \par \uc2  Analysts have said the level of 2.05 reais per dollar became an informal floor for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped up its market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the real weakened past that level. \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Michael O'Boyle, Editing by Gary Crosse)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) (REPEAT) | ABN | D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120607e864001e2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
