\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  has no target for  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  -sources\b0\par\par\uc2 546 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2012\par 18:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at limiting \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility\par \par \uc2 * Gov't won't draw lines it cannot defend in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market\par \par \uc2 * Cenbank early Friday action to show "we're in charge"\par \par \uc2 (Adds comments from second government source, byline)\par \par \uc2 By Brian Winter and Patricia Duarte\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, May 25 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market were aimed at limiting volatility after the real depreciated with "excessive" speed, but do not signal a government target range for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , two senior officials told Reuters on Friday.\par \par \uc2 "The strategy is to prevent movements that are too fast and could distort the economy," one official said on condition of anonymity.\par \par \uc2 "On the other hand, we're also not going to draw any hard lines or do anything that over time we cannot defend" in the event of a strong market shock, such as a deterioration of the euro zone crisis, the official said.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began attempting to limit the real's losses on May 18 by selling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps - which essentially increase the supply of dollars in the market. At the time, the real was rapidly depreciating, mostly because of concerns over the euro zone crisis.\par \par \uc2 The real touched a three-year low of around 2.10 per dollar on Wednesday, but swap sales since then have helped push the real back through the 2 per dollar threshold on Friday.\par \par \uc2 In a more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy on Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered to sell swaps at the beginning of the session, when the real traded practically flat against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "That was to show we are in charge," a second official said, also on condition of anonymity.\par \par \uc2 That source, who is a member of President Dilma Rousseff's economic team, said the recent volatility in the real had started to hamper Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 "When the market starts to become dysfunctional, exporters and importers walk away," the official said. "We can't allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to be without a price reference."\par \par \uc2 Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real remains about 15 percent weaker than it was on March 1, making it one of the world's worst-performing major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  over that period.\par \par \uc2 That sell-off was mainly a result of heightened concerns over the external scenario rather than lack of liquidity in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the second source said.\par \par \uc2 The first official also denied market speculation that Rousseff's government was trying to establish a new floor that would prevent the real from depreciating beyond 2.05 or 2.10 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The official said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was, instead, designed to keep the real from sliding too far, too fast, adding that flexibility in the exchange rate may prove necessary if the euro zone crisis deteriorates in coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 "Nobody really knows what's going to happen with Greece, with Europe," the official said. "We're in wait-and-see mode."\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime is technically free-floating, although Rousseff's government has repeatedly taken steps over the past year to manage its trading level.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Chizu Nomiyama, Bernadette Baum, Leslie Adler)\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-REAL/OFFICIAL (UPDATE 2) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | U | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120525e85p0011y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
