\par\par \b \uc2 Brazilian Real Closes Volatile Session Little Changed\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paul Kiernan   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 433 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2012\par 22:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real ended a volatile session not far from where it started but traded in a broad range Thursday, as an early selloff on dour economic sentiment prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a third consecutive session.\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading in Sao Paulo at BRL2.0402 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, slightly stronger than Wednesday's close of BRL2.0419.\par \par \uc2 Following the release of negative data on China's manufacturing base, and an uninspiring effort by European leaders to stimulate economic growth and contain the debt crisis, the real skidded to as weak as BRL2.05 to the dollar in late-morning trading.\par \par \uc2 But an announcement by the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of an auction to sell dollar swap contracts abruptly sent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stronger, and the real briefly approached BRL2.0280 before depreciating gradually over the afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Market participants say the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to gain much ground against the dollar before Greece holds elections on June 17, when voters may effectively choose whether the debt-saddled and austerity-battered nation will stay in the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has signaled a willingness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during sharp sell-offs. The bank has auctioned the equivalent of more than $4 billion in swap contracts since Tuesday, and the real has responded promptly by recovering from intraday lows versus the dollar.\par \par \uc2 This month's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pattern contrasts with that of April, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought billions of dollars in the spot market to push the real weaker against the dollar. Brazilian authorities for the past couple of years have expressed a preference for a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which they say is key to the industrial sector's competitiveness.\par \par \uc2 Barclays\uc2  Emerging Markets Research said the local government's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 --not only in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but also in the form of price controls on gasoline and pressure on banks to reduce loan spreads--has "pushed investors to the sidelines."\par \par \uc2 "Markets love to hate Brazil today," \uc2 Barclays\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 But the firm added that investors' pessimism about a recent slowdown in the Brazilian economy is "overblown," as growth should pick up in the second half of the year.\par \par \uc2 "We would expect--global context permitting--some market optimism to re-emerge, though with less intensity than in the past," \uc2 Barclays\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 -By Paul Kiernan, Dow Jones Newswires; (+55)11-3544-7074, paul.kiernan@dowjones.com [ 24-05-12 2006GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120524e85o0013p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
