\par\par \b \uc2 Fund Manager Balances Brazil Yields With  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2 , Policy Risks\b0\par\par\uc2 629 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 2012\par 16:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --ING's Michael Mata feels compelled to hold Brazilian paper for its high yields\par \par \uc2 --But Global Bond Fund co-manager has been cutting exposure to and hedging real since March\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Erin McCarthy and Prabha Natarajan \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--ING fund manager Michael Mata finds himself in a curious paradox when it comes to Brazil: He dislikes the government's constantly changing policies, but feels compelled to hold Brazilian paper for its uniquely high yields.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Brazilian real, however, is another story. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  offers him a chance to express his view. Mata, who co-manages the ING Global Bond Fund with $734 million in assets under management, has been cutting his exposure to and hedging the Brazilian real since March, when the real started retreating from some of the strongest levels seen this year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mata's approach to Brazil represents the fence many longer-term investors have to straddle: local bonds' attractive yields in a low-rate world and a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  burdened by a government and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  determined to weaken it. Since March, the Brazilian real has dived 19% against the dollar to three-year lows after the Brazilian government began a series of measures to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . During this time, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  directly in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to weaken the real.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors have begun to question the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's role in the easing, Mata said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Certainly, investors' perception of Brazil is that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has become completely politicized," he said, adding that it no longer is focused only on controlling inflation but also has taken on the government's pro-growth push.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rolling 12-month inflation in Brazil is at 5.05% as of mid-May, above the government's official central target of 4.5%. But analysts warn that the easing measures could push it to around 5.2% by year end and as much as 5.60% by 2013.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has "certainly lost some credibility with markets, and that's reflected in the value of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," Mata said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Since Friday, the Brazilian real has been on a weakening spiral triggered by poor liquidity in its markets, and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has had to step in and sell dollars to slow the real's excessive losses.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite the confusing moves and lack of clarity in direction, Mata has maintained the fund's "decent-sized position" in short-dated, Brazilian local-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  government bonds. He expects Brazil to continue to cut rates, by another 25 to 50 basis points. In recent months, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has slashed the key Selic rate to a historic low of 9%, from 11% at the start of the year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We're close to the end of the easing cycle," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The fund, for instance, currently has exposure to local-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bonds maturing in 2014, which were recently yielding more than 8%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mata typically doesn't hedge the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exposure on such debt. But, recently, he has hedged out most of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risk through non-deliverable forwards, and nearly all of the rate risk, using interest-rate swaps, he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mata is unsure of his next move in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Latin America's most dominant economy. He would like to buy the real, but speculation that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central-bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy could become more aggressive than expected is giving him caution, he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There is some policy risk there that rates go even lower, which would weaken the real," he added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Erin McCarthy, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2712; erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com and Prabha Natarajan, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2468; prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com @djfxtrader [ 05-23-12 1010ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020120523e85n0003h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
