\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Dominates Emerging Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Trading; Debt Steady\b0\par\par\uc2 521 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2012\par 22:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen or suspected in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  and South Korea\par \par \uc2 --Broader global risks keep investors cautious\par \par \uc2 --Emerging market debt little changed\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Erin McCarthy \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  see-sawed Friday, driven primarily by external sources and triggering \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central-bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in some markets.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was in the spotlight as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surprised markets by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  late Friday afternoon to curb the Brazilian real's losses. Up until this point, Brazilian authorities had been taking a variety of measures to weaken the real.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors ultimately took on an overall cautious tone ahead of this weekend's Group of Eight meeting, as concerns about the euro-zone sovereign-debt crisis still loomed over markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We're not in deep contagion mode; we've moved away from deep risk," said Sebastien Galy, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2 . But investors would "rather stick to mostly risk-off positions ahead of the weekend," he added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Heavy demand for dollars onshore in Brazil drove the real down more than 2% intraday Friday to its weakest levels since May 2009, taking out stop-losses for local players that had bullish bets on Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders said. The rapid, uncontrolled move downward in the real spurred Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sell the equivalent of $654.3 million in dollar swap contracts, much to the surprise of markets. Previously, Brazilian officials indicated they were comfortable with the dollar trading around BRL2. The dollar shot up to BRL2.0539, but later traded at BRL2.0223, after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped in.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In South Korea, suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities prevented a further slide for the won, which hit a five-month low against the dollar. The dollar bought KRW1,169 late Friday, easing back from KRW1,175.4 seen earlier in the session, according to CQG.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indian rupee was also in focus, falling to a record low against the U.S. dollar for a third straight session Friday before a recovery in local stocks and the euro pulled it into positive territory. The dollar traded as high as INR54.91 Friday, but later traded at INR54.40. India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been seen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily in the market in recent weeks to arrest the rupee's relentless slide against the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Russian ruble was another underperformer Friday, hit by falling oil prices. Since Russia is the world's second-largest producer of crude oil, the ruble often mimics moves in oil prices. The dollar changed hands at RUB31.305 from RUB31.073 late Thursday, according to CQG.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Emerging market sovereign debt, however, was little changed on the day, in line with benchmark U.S. Treasurys, which also were largely steady. The spread on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  Emerging Markets Bond Index Global, or Embig, widened by two basis points. In price terms, the index slipped 0.3%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Erin McCarthy, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2712; erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com @djfxtrader\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Sudeep Jain contributed to this article. [ 18-05-12 2020GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120518e85i00100\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
