\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Surprises With  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  To Steady Real\b0\par\par\uc2 653 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2012\par 22:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent further \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness\par \par \uc2 --Investors snap up dollar swap contracts, equivalent to $654 million\par \par \uc2 --Traders not clear whether this was to prevent a panic, or to indicate a ceiling\par \par \uc2 By Matthew Cowley\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with a move to try to stem some of the Brazilian real's losses, as the euro zone's sovereign debt crisis continues to roil global markets.\par \par \uc2 Although there'd been speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might step into the market at some point, given the recent weakness, some investors had let down their guard after the government signaled that it was quite content with the real's losses, as it helps industry and exporters.\par \par \uc2 On Friday afternoon, however, some traders reported heavy selling of the real by local investors in Brazil, which was starting to spiral out of control. The shrinking flow of dollars into the country created a liquidity gap, which led to a rapid depreciation by the real, market participants said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had plunged more than 2% against the dollar when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market offering to sell dollar swap contracts at auction. It's the first time it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in three weeks; previously, however, it had been trying to deter real strength.\par \par \uc2 Traders weren't clear whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was signaling a ceiling for the real, at BRL2.05 per dollar, or whether it was simply stepping in to provide support in a market which was starting to become--in the jargon of the market--"disorderly."\par \par \uc2 According to Jankiel Santos, of BES Investimentos, the move on Friday to weaken the real was speculative, with traders testing the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's patience and trying to gauge at which level it feels it needs to step in. "There may be further \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Santos said. "With the global scene continuing to weigh, there's going to be more of the same in coming days. They could even sell dollars on the spot market."\par \par \uc2 The impact of the auction was immediate, with the real retracing to BRL2.03 per dollar, and then taking another leg down to BRL2.0155, according to Tullett Prebon via Factset. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still nearly 1% weaker on the day, from BRL1.9974 in late trading on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold all 13,000 of the dollar-swap contracts on offer, equivalent to $654.3 million, according to a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement.\par \par \uc2 The dollar-swap auctions offer investors the opportunity to exchange contracts indexed to domestic interest rates for paper linked to the U.S. dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  typically holds \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap auctions at a time when the Brazilian real is weakening against the U.S. dollar. The auctions often help to stem the depreciation of the real by offering investors the chance to obtain contracts linked to the U.S. dollar at a time of dollar scarcity.\par \par \uc2 Friday's dollar swap is the first since Oct. 28.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  marks a turnaround for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Until recently, it had been buying up dollars, encouraging weakness in the Brazilian real, which the government has claimed is overvalued against the dollar. The last time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to buy dollars was April 27.\par \par \uc2 As the euro-zone crisis intensified, however, the Brazilian real has been among the hardest hit in emerging markets. Although the government has welcomed the weakness as a boost for Brazilian industry and exporters, there had been speculation that any signs of a sudden collapse in the real could prompt \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 -By Matthew Cowley, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11-3544-7090; brazil@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 --Luciana Magalhaes, Paulo Winterstein, Diana Kinch, Prabha Natarajan and Erin McCarthy contributed to this article. [ 18-05-12 2020GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120518e85i000zz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
