\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: RIM Drops Under $11 As Techs Take Drubbing\b0\par\par\uc2 1,223 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2012\par 22:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 4:48 (DowJones) \uc2 Zynga\uc2  (ZNGA) wasn't the only tech company pinched during the \uc2 Facebook\uc2  (FB) IPO frenzy. \uc2 Research in Motion\uc2  (RIMM) continued to slide as well, closing below $11 for the first time in nearly a decade. RIMM drops 3.4% to $10.99, giving it a market cap of $5.8B, or two thirds below its value a year ago. RIMM executives have assured investors that its next line of phones, dubbed BlackBerry 10, will turn the company's fortunes around. But shareholders are losing patience, and analysts speculate that if the stock slides lower, an outside buyer might emerge. (william.connors@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 4:30 (Dow Jones) \uc2 Chesapeake Energy\uc2 's (CHK) board is caving in to investor pressure by cutting compensation for outside directors by 20% and taking away perks -- such as use of the company's fractionally owned aircraft for personal travel. The move comes ahead of a shareholders meeting that promises to be contentious, as shareholders voice discontent over the company's corporate governance. (angel.gonzalez@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 4:10 (Dow Jones) US stocks cap off an ugly week with more declines, and Dow Industrials fall for the 12th session in the last 13, a span that's nicked almost 7% off the index. \uc2 Facebook\uc2 's overhyped IPO flops, adding to the day's disappointment as shares needed concerted support from underwriter buying in order to not close below $38 offering price. FB's social media peers among collateral damage as \uc2 Groupon\uc2  falls 6.7%, LinkedIn sheds 5.5% and \uc2 Zynga\uc2  slides 13%. FB up 0.6% at $38.23. Indeed, Europe remains the millstone around US equities' neck, and won't be easily lifted. DJIA falls 73.11 to 12369.38, and Nasdaq Comp loses 34.90 to 2778.79. S&P 500 ends 9.64 lower at 1295.22. (john.shipman@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 3:57 (Dow Jones) The Brazilian real's further weakening against the dollar has been purely speculative, in a move to test the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gauge at which level it feels it needs to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Espirito Santo Investment Bank says. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  coming at BRL2.05 to the dollar shows the bank's actually quite comfortable with the real at up to that level, BES says. With the global scene continuing problematic, the real's likely to hover around current levels in coming days with further \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  controlling any excesses, according to BES. This could even take the shape of dollar spot sales, BES says. (diana.kinch@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 3:51 (Dow Jones) No official comment yet from Nasdaq (NDAQ) on the continuing headache among traders and brokers regarding \uc2 Facebook\uc2  (FB) IPO, some of whom remain uncertain whether transactions in the newly listed shares stand or not. NDAQ has issued several notices to traders saying that confirmations of transactions have been issued, but representatives have yet to say anything on the matter, hours after the problems first surfaced ahead of FB's shares opening for trade. (jacob.bunge@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 3:37 (Dow Jones) Despite small price pulback Friday, the benchmark 10-year note posts a price gain for the week. The yield fell for a ninth straight week, matching the longest stretch since October 1998. While this is more evidence that the note is overbought and prone to profit-taking, the yield may go lower still on flight to safety. "It is very possible the yield will hit new low if something big were to happen in Europe or some unforeseen geopolitical event were to occur," says Kevin Giddis, head of fixed income at Raymond James/Morgan Keegan. Giddis expects the yield could fall as low as 1.5% but he added that this might not happen over the next week or so, because of the new supply. The 10-year note is 4/32 lower to yield 1.714%, from 1.843% a week ago. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 3:33 (Dow Jones) What had driven the Brazilian real to such rapid losses late Friday afternoon was local players in Brazil who were long BRL, short USD, hitting their stop-losses at key technical levels, a trader says. With locals being taken out of the positions quite heavily, these big local flows resulted in a fairly uncontrolled move in USD/BRL. And to the rescue: the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dollar now trades at BRL2.0371. (erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 3:29 (Dow Jones) Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap auction this afternoon has indicated to the market that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  considers the exchange rate of BRL2.05 to the dollar as the floor for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says Reginaldo Gualhardo, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Sao Paulo's brokerage Treviso. Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold the equivalent of $654.3 million in dollar swap contracts this afternoon. (luciana.magalhaes@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 3:26 (Dow Jones) Bond prices tick down as the euro recently hit a session high vs the dollar. Some traders say the \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling the dollar to prop up the real is part of the boost for the euro, while some investors also pare euro shorts ahead of the G8 meeting this weekend for fear some policy actions may emerge to calm market's nerves. The 10-year note is 5/32 lower to yield 1.718%. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 3:25 (Dow Jones) A confluence of factors has come into play to push the EUR higher: 1) Brazil is selling dollars to boost real, which pushes USD crosses lower, triggering stops in EUR/USD. 2) G8 is meeting this weekend; best to be positioned defensively against euro-supportive words/measures. 3) It's Friday, after a week of heavy euro losses; time to take profits and square positions into weekend. 4) For the same reasons, trading conditions are thin. 5) The euro zone is, for now, still intact. (michael.j.casey@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 3:22 (Dow Jones) While shale gas production is being scaled back, the same can't be said of shale oil, says Eric Butler, executive vice president, Union Pacific Railroad. Shale oil-related freight volume is up 400% as drilling rig counts rose 50% since 2009, he says. "There really is a boom going on in this country in oil drilling which is good for our country, good for our economy and good for our company," he says. (tatyana.shumsky@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 3:19 (Dow Jones) \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprises \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with sudden \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Friday, a clear signal that it wants to draw a line under recent BRL weakness. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did a good job catching most investors off guard--which always hurts the most, and amplifies the impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . BRL comes off the high of BRL2.0524, and trades at BRL2.0347--but is still more than 1% weaker on the day. (matthew.cowley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par To contact the Market Talk Editors, \par Bradley Davis, 212 416-2654, bradley.davis@dowjones.com \par Kevin Kingsbury, 212 416-2354, kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com \par John Shipman, 212 416-2181,john.shipman@dowjones.com \par Patrick Sullivan, 212 416-2326,Patrick.sullivan@dowjones.co \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 05-18-12 1648ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4035   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020120518e85i000ub\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
