\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: For Those Scratching Heads About EUR/USD Surge...\b0\par\par\uc2 958 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2012\par 21:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 3:25 (Dow Jones) A confluence of factors has come into play to push the EUR higher: 1) Brazil is selling dollars to boost real, which pushes USD crosses lower, triggering stops in EUR/USD. 2) G8 is meeting this weekend; best to be positioned defensively against euro-supportive words/measures. 3) It's Friday, after a week of heavy euro losses; time to take profits and square positions into weekend. 4) For the same reasons, trading conditions are thin. 5) The euro zone is, for now, still intact. (michael.j.casey@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 3:22 (Dow Jones) While shale gas production is being scaled back, the same can't be said of shale oil, says Eric Butler, executive vice president, Union Pacific Railroad. Shale oil-related freight volume is up 400% as drilling rig counts rose 50% since 2009, he says. "There really is a boom going on in this country in oil drilling which is good for our country, good for our economy and good for our company," he says. (tatyana.shumsky@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 3:19 (Dow Jones) \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprises \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with sudden \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Friday, a clear signal that it wants to draw a line under recent BRL weakness. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did a good job catching most investors off guard--which always hurts the most, and amplifies the impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . BRL comes off the high of BRL2.0524, and trades at BRL2.0347--but is still more than 1% weaker on the day. (matthew.cowley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 3:11 (Dow Jones) \uc2 Facebook\uc2  (FB) traded 460M shares by 3:07pm EDT, the most ever for a US stock the day of its IPO. The prior record-holder was GM, which saw 458M shares trade the day it went public in 2010, after coming out of bankruptcy. Much of the FB trading -- 100M shares' worth, in fact -- occurred in the first few minutes after the stock opened. (alexandra.scaggs@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 3:03 (Dow Jones) The euro popped up to a fresh session high of $1.2742 as NY trading winds down. Traders say the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been supported today by covering of short positions after its dramatic move below $1.27 this week. After touching below the $1.2650 target in earlier trading, some investors begin unwinding long-standing bets against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says Bob Sinche at RBS. Euro recovery has helped snap a 14-day streak of gains in the ICE dollar index. (matt.walter@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 3:01 (Dow Jones) The Central Reserve Bank of Peru sold two series of US dollar repos in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, as banks sought the greenback to meet increased reserve requirements. On Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time placed the US dollar denominated instruments, adding $50M in liquidity. On Friday, it placed $400M in two series of the new repos, one for three days and the other for seven days. (robert.kozak@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2:59 (Dow Jones) Most of the crude oil shuttled across the US is transported through pipelines, but there's a faster way of getting oil around, says Union Pacific (UNP) executive Eric Butler. And wouldn't you know, he says it's his industry. "We move crude faster by rail than it moves through a pipeline." So while pipelines dominate the volume, "rail has the speed advantage." (tatyana.shumsky@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2:55 (Dow Jones) Front-month Nymex natural-gas futures go at a 4-month settlement high amid forecasts of warmer-than-normal temperatures the next 2 weeks. That ratchets up expectations for natural-gas demand from power plants as more consumers are liable to switch on the air conditioners. The latest gain also triggered a round of short-covering going into the weekend. Nymex June natural-gas futures jump 5.7% to $2.742/MMBtu. (ben.lefebvre@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2:51 (Dow Jones) Even if traders did not add any new speculative bets on the CME this week, positioning will still show some movement thanks to the dollar's big rally in recent weeks. Exchange rates add a second layer to the shift in positioning each week beyond the change in the number of net contracts, so with the dollar's big rally, extreme short or long bets on a foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar wouldn't look as big this week. For example, if the number of net short contracts betting on the euro to fall against the dollar does not change at all, the speculative positioning as valued in dollars would drop some 2% to $22.9B because of the dollar's gains. (stephen.bernard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2:49 (Dow Jones) CFTC data due out later today could show that speculative bets that the euro will fall might be approaching fresh records. The steep decline in the spot price of the EUR/USD in the past two weeks could be an indication that traders are further ramping up bets on a euro drop. If the net euro short position climbs above $28.1B, that would be the highest level since at least 2007 when CFTC data became available. Speculative traders held a net short euro position of $23.4B as of May 8. Data due later will reflect positioning as of May 15. (stephen.bernard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par To contact the Market Talk Editors, \par Bradley Davis, 212 416-2654, bradley.davis@dowjones.com \par Kevin Kingsbury, 212 416-2354, kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com \par John Shipman, 212 416-2181,john.shipman@dowjones.com \par Patrick Sullivan, 212 416-2326,Patrick.sullivan@dowjones.co \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 05-18-12 1525ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4035   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020120518e85i000lg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
