\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  fall on Greece, real hits 2/dlr\b0\par\par\uc2 510 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2012\par 19:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Traders in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculate c. bank will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real off 0.55 pct, Mexico's peso down 0.68 pct\par \par \uc2 By Danielle Fonseca and Rachel Uranga\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY, May 14 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened on Tuesday w ith Brazil's real closing at a near three-year low, fueling speculation the country's bank could soon \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Worries that new elections in Greece would harden domestic opposition to an international bailout and open the possibility that the country could exit the euro weighed on global markets and pushed Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to its weakest level since July 2009.\par \par \uc2 "The market is seeing the possibility of Greece leave the euro zone as very likely," said Alfredo Barbutti, chief economist at BCG Liquidez.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real weakened 0.55 percent to 2 p er dollar.\par \par \uc2 Some investors have been pushing the real above the level of 2 per dollar to test the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tolerance of a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that could spur inflation by raising import prices.\par \par \uc2 "We have some speculation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market right now," said Reginaldo Galhardo, a manager at Treviso brokerage in Sao Paulo. "The market is wondering whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so it is pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 2 per dollar."\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars in the spot market from February to April, helping weaken the exchange rate from around 1.7 per dollar, which was considered harmful to exporters.\par \par \uc2 Some traders bet the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if the real weakens beyond 2 per dollar. Government officials have indicated they still do not anticipate meaningful inflationary pressures from the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at that level.\par \par \uc2 "At between 2 and 2.10, the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is really, really high," said Diego Donadio, Latin America \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and debt strategist for \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican and Chilean pesos hit four month lows as a ttempts to form a new government in Greece collapsed spooking investors and raising the prospect anti-bailout candidates could sweep elections, sparking a fresh round of the euro-zone crisis.\par \par \uc2 The news from Greece weighed on riskier Latin American assets that tend to sell off when investors seek safety in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso weakened 0.68 percent to 13.8350 per dollar. C hile's peso fell to four month lows, nearing 500 per dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed 1.42 percent weaker to bid at 499.30 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The 500 level is really difficult to break," said Francisco Schneider, director of trading at Celfin Capital in Santiago. "If it happens the next level could be 504 but if markets calm down, don't rule out the peso's recovery to new ranges between 490 and 500."\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Moises Avila and Froilan Romero in Santiago; Danielle Ramos in Sao Paulo; Editing by Diane Craft)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | U | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120518e85f0014e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
