\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Brazil real at 2 per dlr, 1st time since July 2009\b0\par\par\uc2 269 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 2012\par 19:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Investors testing for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  gov't not worried over real's slide-Mantega\par \par \uc2 (Adds context, details)\par \par \uc2 By Asher Levine\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, May 14 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real weakened sharply in spot trading o n M onday and briefly crossed the 2 per U.S. dollar threshold for the first time since July 2009 as uncertainty over the impact of a potential Greek exit from the euro drove investors away from riskier assets.\par \par \uc2 Comments by Finance Minister Guido Mantega added more pressure to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  o n M onday after he said the real's current weakness should not be considered "worrisome" because it benefits local exporters.\par \par \uc2 The real has slipped around 6.5 percent against the dollar in 2012, following a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar purchases at auction and a fall in Brazil's benchmark interest rate to single-digit levels near record lows.\par \par \uc2 Some investors began pushing the real to the 2-per-dollar threshold early in the session to test whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop it from depreciating and stoking inflation, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president, Alexandre Tombini, said on T hursday that the bank would continue assessing all factors that affect inflation, including the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 By 14:54 p.m. (1754 GMT) the real had lost 1.85 percent to a bid price of 1.9915 to the U.S. dollar.\par \par 