\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Closes Stronger Amid Inflation,  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Concerns\b0\par\par\uc2 479 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2012\par 21:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Real closes sharply stronger against dollar\par \par \uc2 --Real exited active trading at BRL1.9456 to the dollar versus BRL1.9695 Wednesday\par \par \uc2 --Signs of faster inflation sparked concerns \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might sell dollars\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Jeffrey T. Lewis \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BRASILIA (Dow Jones)-The Brazilian real closed stronger against the dollar Thursday amid concern the dollar's recent appreciation might fuel inflationary pressure and push the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by selling greenbacks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real exited active trading at BRL1.9456 to the dollar, stronger than BRL1.9695 Wednesday, a change of 1.2%, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet. Wednesday's close was the weakest for the real in nearly three years.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After strengthening almost 10% against the dollar in the first two months of the year, the real has since given up those gains and more, amid concerns about Europe's sovereign debt crisis and sluggish economic growth in developed countries.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Government and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  intended to weaken the real and protect Brazilian exporters have also played their part. With the recent appreciation of the dollar, the real might have reached a balance point, past which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might feel forced to step in and sell the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , analysts said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It's not in our interest for the dollar to strengthen much more, because it can start to cause problems for inflation," said Paulo Fujisaki, an analyst at the Socopa brokerage in Sao Paulo. "If the real weakens much more than it has, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could step in and start selling dollars."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Wednesday the IBGE statistical agency showed a mild slowing in annual inflation as of April, to 5.10% from 5.24% the previous month. However, the monthly gain was a sharp 0.64%--compared with 0.21% in March--higher than forecast and a warning sign to analysts.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Alexandre Tombini said the April inflation figures don't indicate a reversal in the trend of slowing inflation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Speaking on the sidelines of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's inflation-targeting seminar Thursday, Tombini said that inflation readings in the next three months are expected to come in below April's 0.64%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We are still in the process of converging on the target," Tombini told reporters. Brazil targets an annual inflation rate of 4.5%, with a tolerance of plus or minus two percentage points.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is keeping an eye on weakness in the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which could affect inflation, Tombini said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The dollar is in the process of a global appreciation at the moment," especially in relation to merging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Tombini noted.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Jeffrey T. Lewis, Dow Jones Newswires; +55 61 9278 5267; jeffrey.lewis@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Jeff Fick in Rio de Janeiro contributed to this article [ 10-05-12 1937GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120510e85a001v3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
