 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: High Global Inventories Create Search For Markets\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 11:47 EDT *DJ  Brazil Not Suffering From Deindustrialization -Mantega\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 11:47 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Local Industry Facing Competition From Imports\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 11:48 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Developed Countries Using Monetary Expansion\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 11:49 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Policies Injecting Mountain Of Liquidity\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 11:50 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Global Bank Assets At $9 Tln Vs $3 Tln In 2007\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 11:51 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Excess Resources Head For Countries With Best Conditions\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 11:51 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Countries Like Brazil, Mexico Targets For Capital Flows\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 11:53 EDT *DJ  Brazil To Continue Sustaining Domestic Market -Mantega\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 11:54 EDT *DJ  Brazil To Create More Jobs In 2012 Than 2011 -Mantega\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 11:55 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Low Unemployment Supports Domestic Consumption\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 11:56 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Credit Growth Reducing Velocity, Not Enough To Sustain Growth\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 11:56 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Real Interest Rates Remain High Compared With Other Countries\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 11:57 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Increases In Loan Arrears Normal Given Slowing Economy\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 11:57 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Increased Credit, Lower Spreads Solution For Arrears\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 11:59 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Lower Selic Rate Not Reducing Credit Costs\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 12:00 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Savings Changes Made To Avert Migration By Funds\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 12:05 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Depreciated \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Best For Generating Jobs\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 12:06 EDT *DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Currency Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Came After Call For Talks Ignored\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 12:07 EDT *DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Mantega: Without \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Real Would Now Trade At BRL1.00 To US Dollar\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 12:07 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Real At 1-To-Dollar Would Have Destroyed Local Industry\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 12:08 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Lower Rates, Taxes And \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Have Businesses Smiling\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 12:10 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Sustainable Economy Needs Solid Current Accounts\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 12:10 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Nominal Deficit Should Fall By Half In 2012\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 12:11 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Fighting Inflation Always A Priority\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 12:12 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Additional Sectors Could See Payroll Tax Breaks\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 12:14 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Intensifying Measures To Defend Trade -Mantega\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 12:15 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Trade Protections Will Continue Until Markets Normalize\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 12:15 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Global Economy Should Improve In Two Years\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 12:17 EDT *DJ  Brazil's Mantega: Government Always Worried About \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Rate\par \par \uc2 4 May 2012 12:42 EDT DJ  Brazil Finance Minister: Banking Spreads Remain High\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--The difference between interest rates charged by Brazilian banks and the country's Selic benchmark rate remain too high, an anomaly that needs to be corrected, Finance Minister Guido Mantega said Friday.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at an event in Sao Paulo, Mantega said that state-owned banks have already reduced interest rates. "To reduce spreads, the Selic should continue to fall as long as conditions permit," Mantega said.\par \par \uc2 Increased lending by state-owned banks such as \uc2 Banco do Brasil\uc2  (BBAS3.BR) and Caixa Economica Federal should also help cut banking spreads "because this generates competition," Mantega said. "Competition is the best solution for reducing bank spreads."\par \par \uc2 Brazil announced Thursday measures to remove a key technical barrier to further interest rate cuts by the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The government reduced the fixed interest rate paid out by passbook savings accounts, which is linked to the Selic, so that the Selic could be cut below its historical low of 8.75%.\par \par \uc2 The Selic currently stands at 9%, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has indicated a willingness to further cut interest rates.\par \par \uc2 "Real interest rates at 2% are a dream every Brazilian should have because everyone will have credit available for buying," Mantega said. "When this moment arrives, it will mean that inflation is under control."\par \par \uc2 Mantega addressed concerns that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have turned its back on the fight against inflation, saying that inflation is "always a priority."\par \par \uc2 "The Selic will only fall if inflation is totally under control," Mantega said. Inflation is currently on a downward trend headed for a rate of 4.5% to 5% in 2012, the finance minister added.\par \par \uc2 Despite the changes to interest rates paid out by savings accounts, Mantega said the passbooks remain the best alternative for small savers. "The 100 million small savers should continue [with passbooks] because they have a good return," Mantega said.\par \par \uc2 Brazilians will also benefit by the move because lower interest rates will mean greater access to home loans at much cheaper rates, Mantega added.\par \par \uc2 --By Rogerio Jelmayer and Jeff Fick, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-21-2586-6085; Jeff.Fick@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 04, 2012 12:42 ET (16:42 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120504e854004fg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
