\par\par \b \uc2 Why \uc2 Wells Fargo\uc2 's Norris, Emerging-Market Peers Are On The Sidelines\b0\par\par\uc2 743 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Mai 2012\par 21:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Fund manager is waiting for clearer picture on the global economy to emerge\par \par \uc2 --Norris still prefers emerging-market assets in longer term\par \par \uc2 --Fund remains overweight emerging-market debt but has hedged \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure in some countries\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Erin McCarthy and Prabha Natarajan \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--In the struggle that goes on in Tony Norris's mind, his cautionary bent has won out again.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The co-manager of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wells Fargo Advantage International\f28 \uc2 \f2  Bond Fund has decided he will wait for more positive signs from global economies in the coming weeks and months before adding emerging-market assets to his portfolio.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Norris isn't alone in this position. He belongs to a significant camp of investors who missed out on emerging markets' strong early-2012 rally but remain hesitant to wade back in even after those assets have fallen to cheaper values, despite that they describe themselves as long-term emerging-market bulls.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 They are waiting for the dust to settle and a clearer picture to emerge on China's slowdown, on Europe's sovereign issues and on the course of the U.S. economy. Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have been in a lull in recent weeks and continue to move in correlation with investor confidence.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With Asian powerhouses India and China facing decelerating rates of growth, with Brazil's government weakening its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to boost its exports growth, and with many advanced countries painfully working down their budget deficits, investors' outlook toward emerging markets has dimmed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 However, Norris believes by mid-year, emerging-market assets including \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can bounce back. He has a bearish dollar view that supports that outlook.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The long-term negative for the U.S. is the twin deficits," he said, referring to fiscal and current-account deficits. "The short-term story is better relative growth."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That was the outlook of his fund at the start of the year, and it was positioned for a rough ride, especially in the first quarter, on expectations of a default from Greece on its debt payments. But emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rallied sharply in the first few months of the year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Of late, most of the verve of that run has fizzled out. That is why Norris and his team are watching all the signs--economic-data releases, oil prices and market sentiment--in the coming weeks to guide the course of his portfolio of $1.73 billion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A more-positive backdrop could lead to additional exposure to emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and nonsovereign-emerging-market debt like corporate and high-yield bonds, Norris said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 However, he added one "major move" this year has been a shift in emphasis in the euro zone from the core to peripheral economies, after the region's improvement in sentiment following the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's liquidity measures. In 2011, the fund had zero exposure to Italy and Spain, but this year it moved to a neutral position, Norris said. Despite the recent escalation of concerns on Spain, his team has decided to hold steady.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The fund remains broadly overweight emerging-market debt but it has hedged \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exposure in various markets to guard against \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  volatility. That view extends to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , where a series of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventionist\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  measures from the government and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have curbed the Brazilian real's appreciation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The fund is still overweight Brazilian debt but it began hedging the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in early March when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  accelerated its easing program with a rate cut of 75 basis points to 9.75%, Norris said. Since then, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has eased by another 75 basis points and left the option open for more cuts. Norris prefers Brazilian global bonds that can be settled through foreign clearing-settlement system Euroclear.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Our view on Brazil is it's a long-term value play," he said, adding with the "real yield available on Brazilian bonds, it's still one of the best value areas in the world."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Elsewhere in emerging markets, the fund is overweight Mexico, Czech Republic, Poland, South Korea and Malaysia, Norris said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "If one looks at \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  year to date, small economies that have a better growth outlook have been the best performing," he said. "Over the longer term those \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will continue to outperform."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Erin McCarthy and Prabha Natarajan, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2712; erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com; @djfxtrader [ 02-05-12 1952GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120502e852001bn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
