\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Closes Stronger, Gains Muted By  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Risk\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paul Kiernan   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 399 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2012\par 22:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's settled barely stronger against the dollar after range-bound trading Friday, as the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by local authorities limited the carryover of positive investor sentiment from other \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading at BRL1.8837 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, compared with BRL1.8845 at Thursday's close.\par \par \uc2 A below-forecast 2.2% expansion in U.S. gross domestic product during the first quarter raised expectations among some investors that the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  might implement more monetary easing to shore up the economy. Friday's GDP report followed comments by Fed Chairman Ben Bernanke earlier this week indicating the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stands ready to use monetary stimulus to support job growth if necessary.\par \par \uc2 Such measures, known as quantitative easing, increase the money supply and tend to pressure the greenback weaker against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dollar rivals such as the euro, Japanese yen and British pound all gained Friday, as did the Mexican peso, which got a boost when the Bank of Mexico held off on cutting interest rates in a monetary policy decision.\par \par \uc2 Win Thin, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at New York's \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2 , said such behavior in international markets would normally be reflected in gains by the Brazilian real.\par \par \uc2 But Brazil's Finance Ministry and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have become more successful at limiting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation this year than in the past, as a range of new taxes targeting \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions have been aided by lower interest rates. The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  almost daily, buying dollars off the market in unannounced spot auctions and sending the real weaker.\par \par \uc2 Late in Friday's session, the bank bought an undisclosed amount of dollars for BRL1.8850 in a spot auction.\par \par \uc2 "It's too early to say people are throwing in the towel on the real," Thin said, adding that the macro factors such as the European debt crisis may be weighing on Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  more than some market participants realize. "I think it's going to be key to see what happens when emerging-market interest really comes back."\par \par \uc2 -By Paul Kiernan, Dow Jones Newswires; (+55)11-3544-7074; paul.kiernan@dowjones.com [ 27-04-12 2020GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120427e84r001sv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
