\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil wants  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  around 1.90/dlr -source\b0\par\par\uc2 483 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 April 2012\par 22:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Brazil gov't wants \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around 1.90/dlr - source\par \par \uc2 * Pushing real closer to 2/dlr seen too costly\par \par \uc2 * Real is one of world's weakest \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year\par \par \uc2 By Patricia Duarte\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, April 24 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government sees a "window of opportunity" to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and maintain the real around the 1.90 per U.S. dollar level, although it will likely not seek to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  much further than that, a senior economic official told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The real has weakened about 9 percent against the dollar since March. It has been one of the weakest performers among major world \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, due to a combination of government action, Brazil's falling interest rates, and continued concern about the economic crisis in Europe.\par \par \uc2 The real closed official trading on Tuesday at about 1.88 per dollar following a session in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased dollars in the spot market. Such measures, plus new government taxes on financial transactions passed earlier this year, have had the net effect of weakening what was one of the world's most overvalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout 2011.\par \par \uc2 President Dilma Rousseff has accused the United States and European nations of waging a "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war" by deploying very accommodative monetary policy. She has said Brazil will defend itself to prevent the resulting wave of foreign capital from damaging its economy.\par \par \uc2 The official, speaking on condition of anonymity to frankly discuss the rationale behind government policy, said that Brazil is trying to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  now because it believes inflationary risks are low and it anticipates foreign capital flows will pick up again later in 2012.\par \par \uc2 "What we see is a window of opportunity for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to achieve, without great risks or stress," an exchange rate of about 1.90 versus the dollar, the official said.\par \par \uc2 The official said that pushing the real closer to the 2 per dollar level was not part of the government's plans for now.\par \par \uc2 "It would require stronger action," the official said.\par \par \uc2 The official added that no new kinds of measures to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  are planned at this time.\par \par \uc2 The real has not been weaker than 1.90 per dollar since briefly puncturing that threshold in November.\par \par \uc2 Traders say the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's short-term direction could depend more on global risk aversion related to the euro zone crisis than government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy has experienced little to no growth since the second half of last year, a slowdown that Rousseff and other officials have blamed partly on the strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, remaining inflationary pressures in Brazil's economy may also be deterring officials from trying to push the real to the 2 per dollar level.\par \par \uc2 (Writing by Brian Winter; Editing by Andrew Hay)\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 / | ABN | M | D | E | RBN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120427e84o001yt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
