\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Opens Stronger As Overseas Bond Sales Cheer Market\b0\par\par\uc2 571 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 April 2012\par 14:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Brazil's real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opens trading stronger on successful EU bond sales\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market players cautious, await minutes from Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting\par \par \uc2 --Brazilian real opens trading at BRL1.8770, stronger from Monday's close at BRL1.8810\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Jeff Fick \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  opened stronger Tuesday as successful bond sales in several troubled European Union countries boosted investor sentiment ahead of the release of several economic indicators.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil's real tracked gains in overseas market, including the euro's rise against the U.S. dollar, traders said. The real opened at BRL1.8770 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet. That was stronger from Monday's close at BRL1.8810. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  later strengthened further to trade at BRL1.8757 to the greenback as of 1224 GMT.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Overall, the mood is still risk averse, still dominated by Europe's unchanging woes," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a morning note to clients.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As has often been the case during the ongoing European sovereign debt crisis, Tuesday's session once again kicked off with positive signs. Italy, the Netherlands and Spain all held bond successful bond sales although there were still some signs of weakness, traders said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Dutch issue, which came a day after the country's government fell, saw interest rates fall on two-year notes but rise on 25-year bonds. Italy and Spain, meanwhile, paid a higher price to attract investors to a debt rollover auction as yields climbed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In Brazil, the latest inflation reading is unlikely to derail the Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent rate-cutting cycle, traders said. The midmonth IPCA-15 consumer price index rose 0.43% through mid-April compared with a 0.25% advance in the same period through mid-March.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Key categories showed signs of accelerating in April, including food prices and housing costs, according to the data.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The latest inflation figure will heighten already intense interest in the meetings from the latest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meeting last week, when the bank reduced the benchmark Selic base interest rate to 9.0%. The bank left the door open for future cuts, saying in its accompanying policy statement that "the risks to inflation are still limited" while noting the "fragility of the global economy."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Lower local interest rates are expected to reduce Brazil's lure for investors seeking higher rates of return, thereby reducing pressure on the real to strengthen.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market players are anxious to glean any indication about the future direction of interest rates from the minutes of the meeting, which will be released Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will likely take direction from the release of several economic indicators both here and abroad, including Brazil's March current account figures. In the U.S., data on home sales prices will be released and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  begins its latest policy meeting.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , market players will be on the lookout for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The bank has been especially active in recent weeks, snapping up dollars in spot-market purchases and restarting sales of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reverse swap contracts. Government officials have also continued the saber-rattling over possible measures aimed at containing the real's recent strength.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Jeff Fick, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-21-2586-6085; Jeff.Fick@dowjones.com [ 24-04-12 1234GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120424e84o000y1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
