\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging-Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 , Debt Lag On Signs Of Weaker Global Growth\b0\par\par\uc2 By Prabha Natarajan   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 575 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 2012\par 21:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and debt weakened Monday on escalating concerns about Europe and outcome of the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's meeting this week.\par \par \uc2 It didn't help that in the first round of French elections, President Nicolas Sarkozy trailed opposition candidate Francois Hollande; an upset could threaten existing ties in Europe.\par \par \uc2 Most emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  trailed the euro's movement, as it fell more than 0.53% per dollar on the day.\par \par \uc2 The dollar gained the most against emerging-European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Hungarian forint, the Czech koruna and the Polish zloty all weakened, with the dollar gaining more than one percentage point against each of these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Hungary Prime Minister Viktor Orban is on a visit to Brussels to meet with European Union officials and to make a case for his country to get the backstop support it seeks from the International Monetary Fund and European Union.\par \par \uc2 The euro once again edged close to HUF300, but backed off at HUF299.94. Tuesday, Orban has a critical meeting with Jose Manuel Barroso, president of the European Commission, to discuss a potential loan agreement.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the collapse of budget talks in Holland and poor manufacturing data from Europe that pointed to a recession were enough to push for dollar strength.\par \par \uc2 Investors are keeping an eye on the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's open-market committee meeting, which could provide markets with clarity on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would provide additional liquidity. Until then, emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are likely to trade in this limited range.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weren't spared. The dollar slipped more than 0.5% against the Mexican peso, Brazilian real and Chilean peso during the day.\par \par \uc2 Investor interest in emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has dropped to subdued levels, \uc2 HSBC\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists said in a note. This is specifically true for Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which have been hurt by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Peru and Colombia. Foreign investors' position on the Brazilian real returned to neutral, \uc2 HSBC\uc2  data showed. But Mexico was an outlier, with foreign holdings of local debt increasing in March on the belief that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained undervalued. The Mexican peso, however, has been weighed down by global concerns and the dollar is trading at MXN13.1999, up 0.75% on the day.\par \par \uc2 The dollar, meanwhile, is trading at BRL1.8834, up 0.63% against the Brazilian real.\par \par \uc2 The volatility of the South Africa's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and its capital inflows and outflows are a big concern, the country's finance minister, Pravin Gordhan, said in an interview. He is watching the weakening of the real and Brazil's counter moves to curb capital flows, but doesn't believe one country can do it alone.\par \par \uc2 "We require global measures," he said, adding this was a much-discussed topic at the recent International Monetary Fund spring meeting in Washington, D.C. The dollar is trading ZAR7.8478 against the rand, up nearly 0.5% on the day.\par \par \uc2 Debt issued by emerging-market sovereigns was mostly wider with risk premiums on the \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2  Emerging Market Bond Index Global weakening by four basis points to 358 basis points over comparable Treasury yields. Risk premiums on Hungary widened by 17 basis points to 639 basis points.\par \par \uc2 -By Prabha Natarajan, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2468; prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com; @djfxtrader [ 23-04-12 1918GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120423e84n0016g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
