\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Closes Stronger As  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Renews  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 865 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 April 2012\par 22:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Brighter outlook abroad helps \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  real gain against U.S. dollar\par \par \uc2 --Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  enters market to buy dollars after one-day respite\par \par \uc2 --Brazilian real exits active trading at BRL1.8703 to the dollar\par \par \uc2 By Jeff Fick\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real recovered from a sharp sell-off the previous session to end stronger Friday, despite the return of Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and renewed rhetoric from government officials\par \par \uc2 The real tracked gains in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar, which gave up ground as economic data from Europe painted an improving picture of the single-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bloc's economy. The real exited active trading at BRL1.8703 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet. That was stronger from Thursday's closing quote at BRL1.8859 to the greenback.\par \par \uc2 Solid economic data from Europe helped kick off the session, boosting investor sentiment, traders said. German business confidence advanced in April, according to the Ifo Institute's latest index. The survey rose to 109.9 in April from 109.8 in March, while the current assessment index surprisingly increased to 117.5 from 117.4. U.K. retail sales also surged last month, rising 1.8% from February, well above expectations of a 0.8% increase.\par \par \uc2 The recent success of bond sales in Spain and Italy also helped ease recent concerns that troubles in the two countries could be a repeat of last year's Greek drama, said Reginaldo Galhardo, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Sao Paulo trading house Treviso.\par \par \uc2 "People are returning to Europe to recoup losses or lock in profits," Galhardo said.\par \par \uc2 Investors are also hopeful that the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  will complete a deal to expand its financial resources to stem the threat of contagion from the euro-zone debt crisis. Better-than-expected earnings from U.S. heavyweights \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  (MSFT) and \uc2 General Electric\uc2  (GE) also led to a brighter outlook.\par \par \uc2 Europe's troubles, however, remain squarely in focus. French elections on Sunday are overhanging the market as the cost of insuring the country's bonds against default climbed higher. Socialist candidate Francois Hollande, who has questioned the country's austerity measures, appears to be leading incumbent Nicolas Sarkozy in the race to be France's president.\par \par \uc2 But the biggest shadow overhanging Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market remains the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and its recent string of heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Galhardo said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sat out Thursday's session, when the real approached the BRL1.90-to-the-dollar mark. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened after Wednesday's expected interest rate cut, which reduced the Selic benchmark rate to 9.0%.\par \par \uc2 "The real has been under pressure from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and also because of the new taxes the bank has imposed in recent months," Galhardo said.\par \par \uc2 Thursday's respite broke a string of five-consecutive sessions in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had held not one but two daily spot-market auctions. With the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's absence, traders picked up the game of cat-and-mouse with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  by driving the real to a session high near BRL1.86 during Friday's session. That was the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trigger, with the bank jumping into the spot market to buy an undisclosed volume of dollars for BRL1.8710 to the greenback.\par \par \uc2 "The market is trying to discover at what rate the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Galhardo said. "It's a question of balance to find the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants the market to stabilize."\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Guido Mantega, taking part in the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  and World Bank spring meetings in Washington this weekend, also renewed the government's rhetoric. Mantega repeated his oft-heard complaints about the use of easy monetary policies in the developed world. Brazil blames low interest rates abroad for the flood of liquidity that has often arrived on the shores of Latin America's biggest economy, where towering interest rates have proved an especially seductive lure.\par \par \uc2 The real's recent weakness, however, was largely attributed to a change in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's most recent policy statement that accompanied Wednesday's interest rate cut. The statement showed that the bank was leaving the door open to further rate cuts with language suggesting that inflation risks in Latin America's largest economy remained low.\par \par \uc2 "The committee notes that until now, given the fragility of the global economy, the contribution of external environment has been disinflationary," the bank said. The statement represented a change in stance from previous minutes, when the bank indicated that it would likely hold rates at a level above the historic low of 8.75%.\par \par \uc2 Given the recent heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and expectations for lower local interest rates, the real appears to have moved to a new level after trading between BRL1.80 and BRL1.83 for several weeks, Galhardo said. Galhardo expects the real to settle in a range between BRL1.85 and BRL1.90 in the near term.\par \par \uc2 -By Jeff Fick, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-21-2586-6085, Jeff.Fick@dowjones.com [ 20-04-12 2004GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120420e84k0013e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
