\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil real leads Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  lower\b0\par\par\uc2 486 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 2012\par 22:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real weakens 1 pct; \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso loses 0.5 pct; Chile peso 0.9 pct weaker\par \par \uc2 * Commodity prices down ahead of Spain's bond sale\par \par \uc2 By Alonso Soto\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, April 18 (Reuters) - Brazil's real slipped to its weakest level this year on Wednesday and became the worst-performing major world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far this month, hit by falling commodity prices and relentless \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The real fell 1 percent to 1.8747 per dollar on Wednesday, after touching its weakest level since Dec. 29. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost nearly 2.7 percent since the start of April, the biggest slide among the world's 36 most traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to Reuters data.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  intensified its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week with two dollar-buying auctions per day, its quickest pace this year, piling onto the weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The auctions are part of the bank's efforts to build up reserves and coincide with the government's battle against the strong local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has cut into exports and hurt local industries with a flood of cheap imports.\par \par \uc2 "A fall in commodity prices abroad, mostly oil, and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has led to a sharp fall of the real versus the dollar," said Luciano Rostagno, chief strategist for Brazil at \uc2 WestLB\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Thomson Reuters-Jefferies CRB Index, a global commodities benchmark, dropped 1 percent on Wednesday as investor risk appetite retreated, hurting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Latin America's major raw material exporters.\par \par \uc2 Renewed focus on the euro zone debt crisis also weighed on Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  a day ahead of a government bond sale in Spain, as the strains on the euro zone drove investors to the perceived safety of the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso weakened 0.5 percent to 13.1616 per dollar, and the Chilean peso shed 0.9 percent to 488.6 per dollar, while remaining in a narrow band that has penned in trading since early March.\par \par \uc2 "There was a lot of caution in the market, with the peso moving between 13.10 and 13.16 per dollar, which is the 100-day moving average, as everyone waits for Spain's auction tomorrow," said Cesar Elizalde, a trader at Banorte-IXE in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 "If it goes badly, we could see the peso at 13.30 per dollar without a problem," he said.\par \par \uc2 The peso has lost about 2.4 percent this month after a sharp rally in the first two months of the year, pressured by concerns about the euro zone debt crisis, patchy economic growth in the United States, and the potential for a sharp slowdown in China.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Rachel Uranga in Mexico City and Brad Haynes in Sao Paulo; Editing by Leslie Adler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  | ABN | E | RBN | D | M | NAT | U   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120421e84i000bn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
