\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Brazil's Real Gives Back Gains of 2012\b0\par\par\uc2 558 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 2012\par 21:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  level in midafternoon trading and comments by Nathan Blanche, partner at consulting firm Tendencias Consultoria.)\par \par \uc2 By Luciana Magalhaes and Rogerio Jelmayer\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--After a strong start in 2012, the real lost ground against the dollar in March and April and gave back all gains saw this year, as the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has played a key role in curbing the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation.\par \par \uc2 To contain the real's almost 10% gains against the dollar in the beginning of the year, Brazilian authorities have stepped up \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Treasury has also issued a sovereign bond denominated in reais in the international market this week, in part to help in the fight against the real appreciation.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real traded earlier today at the BRL 1.866 level, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at BRL1.8664 at the end of 2011. In mid-afternoon session Wednesday, the Brazilian real was trading at BRL1.877 per dollar in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 Foreign direct investment and financial flows to Brazil's high-yielding capital markets have drawn dollars to the emerging economy. Brazil's president, Dilma Rousseff, has been a vocal defender of lower interest rates, to reduce the costs of financing in Brazil and to make Brazilian assets less attractive to foreigners.\par \par \uc2 Even though in an easing cycle, Brazilian interest rates currently stand at 9.75% a year, while rates in the U.S. and Europe are near zero. Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to cut the so-called Selic benchmark rate to 9% later Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "The market is on the hands of the government", said Joao Medeiros, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  director at Sao Paulo brokerage Pioneer Corretora. He said that the market was previously expecting the real to end 2012 at the BRL1.75 level against the greenback. "Now, I think it's possible it will be at around BRL1.90 per dollar, but nobody knows. We have to ask Mantega," he said, referring to Brazil's finance minister, Guido Mantega.\par \par \uc2 "If you make projections based on fundamentals, it's very hard now to know where the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is heading too. It depends on how much the Finance Ministry wants to spend to keep the real from appreciating", said Nathan Blanche, a partner at Sao Paulo-based consulting firm Tendencias Consultoria.\par \par \uc2 "Even with the current level of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did auctions today. They are taking advantage of the lower inflation pressure to keep the real down", Blanche added. Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday bought U.S. dollars at a spot-market in two auctions. The last one at BRL1.880 to the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't reveal the volume of dollars purchased.\par \par \uc2 -By Luciana Magalhaes and Rogerio Jelmayer, Dow Jones Newswires; +5511 3544-7072; luciana.magalhaes@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkbackAmericas@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and 