\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging-Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 , Debt Improve On Rising Confidence\b0\par\par\uc2 By Prabha Natarajan   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 682 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 2012\par 22:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and debt posted sharp gains Tuesday on investors' increased confidence after a strong auction of Spanish bonds and rise in German investor confidence.\par \par \uc2 The South African rand and the Mexican peso led the rally in emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The South African rand rallied after \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  indicated it plans to add South Africa to its world government-bond index Oct. 1.\par \par \uc2 The USD/ZAR is trading at 7.8060, down 1.66% on the day. The index inclusion is expected to lead to a surge in demand for South African bonds in the range of $5 billion to $7.5 billion from portfolio managers. Citi, however, cautioned South Africa would have to keep the size of its outstanding debt above $88 billion. The move by Citi puts South Africa in the same rank as other emerging-market nations in the index including Malaysia, Poland and Mexico.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso also had a similar strong run, with the USD/MXN pair trading at 13.0964, down 0.9% on the day.\par \par \uc2 "Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in general, recovered ground lost in previous session," said Alejandro Cuadrado, head of Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 BBVA\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "However, Brazilian real continued to be the outlier on more \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action, recurrent over the past few sessions," he said.\par \par \uc2 The dollar gained 0.30% on the real to BRL1.8529, pushing the cross much closer to nearly wiping out all the gains it has made so far this year. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also has led to speculation \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be pushing for a dollar level higher than BRL1.80. But \uc2 BBVA\uc2 's Cuadrado expects the USD/BRL pair to hover around the 1.83 to 1.84 level, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  further during bearish sessions.\par \par \uc2 The market also awaits an expected cut of 75 basis points Wednesday on the selic rate, which would help the country prod domestic growth. On a similar theme, India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its interest rates unexpectedly by 50 basis points as a way to spur production and consumption, in a country expected to have its growth rate slacken below 7%.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's announced move to take over the management of energy producer \uc2 YPF SA\uc2  (\uc2 YPF\uc2 , YPFD.BA) continued to reverberate through the markets with risk premiums on the country's bonds weakening by another 16 basis points to 882 basis points over comparable Treasury yields.\par \par \uc2 Other emerging-market debt traded tighter with risk premiums narrowing by seven basis points to 356 basis points over comparable Treasury yields on the \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2  Emerging Market Bond Index Global.\par \par \uc2 Two sovereigns tapped the bond markets Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's National Treasury launched BRL3 billion ($1.6 billion) in sovereign overseas bonds denominated in reais and due 2024, a part of its effort to improve its sovereign-debt profile and the liquidity of sovereign outstanding bonds, a person familiar with the deal said.\par \par \uc2 The bonds were priced with a yield of 8.6%, with proceeds to go toward buying back bonds with shorter maturities. Also, Brazil is offering to pay BRL1,205 for outstanding bonds due 2016 with a face value of BRL1,000, and BRL1,300 for bonds due 2022 with a face value of BRL1,000. The government is seeking to build a real-denominated yield curve similar to the curve of the country's domestically issued debt.\par \par \uc2 The Republic of Indonesia launched a $2 billion, 10-year bond and a $500 million reopening of its 2042 bond, according to investors familiar with the deal. The 10-year bond is set at a yield of 3.85% while the 2042 is at 4.95%, the investors said. Investors are eager for such dollar-denominated debt issued by emerging-market countries, especially those rated at investment grade like Indonesia.\par \par \uc2 -By Prabha Natarajan, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2468; prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 --Rogerio Jelmayer and Paulo Winterstein contributed to this article. [ 17-04-12 2018GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120417e84h0016w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
