\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 , Debt Weakened By Global Concerns\b0\par\par\uc2 By Prabha Natarajan   \par \uc2 OF DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 644 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 April 2012\par 22:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and debt were weaker again as investors' worry about Europe and China escalated. The unexpected decline in U.S. consumer sentiment also weighed on markets.\par \par \uc2 A softer growth in China held emerging markets in check. The country's first quarter growth rate was at an 8.1% annualized rate, lower than expectations of 8.3%. At the same time, investors were too uncertain about Spain and closed positions ahead of the weekend leading to a weakening of yields on the sovereign's debt again.\par \par \uc2 The escalation of global concerns has led investors to scale back their exposure to assets with higher risk and higher returns such as emerging market assets. Many investors are taking profits and closing their positions earlier than expected. In sync with this trend is the outflow of $99 million out of emerging market focused funds in the week ended Wednesday, according to flows from EPFR Global.\par \par \uc2 Much of the outflows were driven by investors exiting local-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and blended funds. This is the second time so far this year that emerging market funds have seen outflows; the previous time was during the week ended Jan. 18.\par \par \uc2 "In light of the global rout and price declines, it is somewhat reassuring that investor flows were not more severe," said David Spegel, global head of emerging markets strategy at ING Financial Markets.\par \par \uc2 "People are starting to kick the tires on their assumptions much earlier in the year," said Cameron Brandt, EPFR's director of research. "Peoples' tendency to sell and go away in May has now just advanced to late March and early April."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the South African rand and the Mexican peso were weaker on the day, with the dollar gaining nearly a 1% on each. The dollar-peso was trading at MXN13.1638, up 1.04% on the day. While the dollar-rand pair was at ZAR7.9397, up 0.85% on the day.\par \par \uc2 Investors, while confident that emerging market economies would fare better than developed markets, expect these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to underperform in the next few months. In the short term, the Brazilian real is expected to keep weakening on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures, and the ruble strengthen on technical support and steady oil prices.\par \par \uc2 Emerging market sovereign bonds were weaker and risk premiums on these bonds widened by five basis points to 360 basis points over comparable Treasury yields on the \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2  Emerging Market Bond Index Global. Risk premiums on Argentina's bonds widened by 13 basis points after reports of the government taking a majority stake on the country's largest energy producer surfaced. Market participants have been asking how the country plans to finance the acquisition.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in other parts of Latin America, central banks of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Peru \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to moderate the pace of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation.\par \par \uc2 Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to keep its key rates unchanged, and use its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a tool to tighten monetary policy, said Benito Berber, an analyst at Nomura. The bank held rates at 4.25% Thursday. Since May 2011, the Peruvian sol's real effective exchange rate or inflation-adjusted value against a basket of peers has appreciated by 5%, mostly engineered by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said. Peru's inflation pressures have eased, and there's little need to change rates.\par \par \uc2 That policy, however, could change if the U.S. Fed embarks on another round of economic stimulus measures termed "quantitative easing," or QE3, Berber said.\par \par \uc2 The dollar-sol pair remains almost unchanged at PEN2.660 on the day after another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 -By Prabha Natarajan and Erin McCarthy, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2468; prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com [ 13-04-12 2016GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120413e84d00112\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
