\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Opens Weaker On Fear Of New Government Measures\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paul Kiernan   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 April 2012\par 15:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real opened slightly weaker Thursday on simmering concerns about the debt crisis in Europe, though lower U.S. jobless claims and easing local inflation softened the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's losses.\par \par \uc2 Recently, the real was quoted in Sao Paulo trading at BRL1.8298 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, compared with its Wednesday close of BRL1.8269.\par \par \uc2 Investor sentiment has soured in recent days due to negative headlines from Spain, where government efforts to reduce a large budget deficit could worsen already high unemployment. Spanish bond yields on Thursday soared to their highest levels since early December after a weak bond auction in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 Protests in debt-crisis epicenter Greece also intensified in the wake of a pensioner's suicide, reportedly in protest of the country's tough austerity measures.\par \par \uc2 A brightening unemployment picture in the U.S. helped to temper the real's depreciation, as weekly claims for jobless benefits fell to their lowest level in four years.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, inflationary pressures continued to ease in March, with the IPCA consumer price index rising 0.21% compared with February's 0.45% increase. The latest figure, which was below market expectations for a 0.36% rise, could allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Brazil to maintain its current cycle of monetary easing.\par \par \uc2 Lower interest rates are generally seen supporting the U.S. dollar. But market participants say a policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and threats by \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Ministry to introduce new measures to halt any significant appreciation have limited the real's upside.\par \par \uc2 "It is hard to say where [authorities] want the real to be, but it's clear it bothers the government every time the exchange rate falls below BRL1.80," said Paulo Fujisaki, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Sao Paulo's Socopa brokerage.\par \par \uc2 -By Luciana Magalhaes, Dow Jones Newswires; +5511 3544-7072; luciana.magalhaes@dowjones.com [ 05-04-12 1335GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120405e845000rl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
