\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Weakens On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears, Europe Concerns\b0\par\par\uc2 593 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2012\par 22:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government has been able to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders at bay with threats to step into exchange markets to prevent a rapid strengthening of the real, but some investors say it may have to back up those promises and take real action soon.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real was little changed Wednesday, weakening slightly against the greenback to BRL1.8269 per dollar, from its previous close of 1.8243. The real has been trading weaker than 1.80 since mid-March on concern the government will levy new taxes on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading--expanding existing taxes or imposing new ones--to curb gains in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "I have to take my hat off to the government," said Ovidio Plinio Soares, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Interbolsa do Brasil, in Sao Paulo. "With numerous threats they've managed to leave the market very anxious, and that's prevented the dollar's decline, although it hasn't been able to strengthen it."\par \par \uc2 Last month the government extended the so-called IOF tax to overseas loans of up to five years, after previously extending it to cover loans of up to three years. In the following days, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to buy up excess dollars in spot or forward auctions.\par \par \uc2 The government has reiterated its commitment to keeping the real at "reasonable" levels in order to help the competitiveness of its industry, but it hasn't announced new measures. More recently, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which used to carry out two auctions a day, has backed off and carried out one auction Tuesday while remaining quiet Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Yet the nervousness remains, reflected in less-volatile trading sessions and a general weakening trend: since the end of February, the real has continually weakened from 1.70. That led a New York-based trader to say that "with the heightened governmental scrutiny, this very novel behavior can have legs," referring to the real's weakening trend.\par \par \uc2 Banco Santander\uc2  noted the "escalating \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " promise could push the real to 1.90 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 But for some, that trend won't depend on government bluster alone, but on government action as well.\par \par \uc2 Threatening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever the real strengthens "has an expiration date," Interbolsa's Soares said. "The time will come when the market will want to challenge the government," at which point policy makers will need a decisive response.\par \par \uc2 So far, Brazil's leaders have yet to test out a response, with bad news from Europe Wednesday quelling appreciation pressures on the real.\par \par \uc2 European markets were in decline after the Spanish government managed to sell just 2.56 billion euros ($3.36 billion) worth of bonds, at the bottom of its planned range, and at yields that were well above previous auctions. Following the auction, yields on 10-year Spanish government debt rose to the highest levels since Jan. 9 on doubts over whether the country will be able to meet a difficult budget deficit target.\par \par \uc2 The rise in Spanish yields, investors worry, could boost yields in other bond markets, testing the euro zone's ability to deal with the higher costs of debt.\par \par \uc2 In the U.S., meanwhile, private-sector payrolls increased 209,000 in March, down from a revised increase of 230,000 in February. The March number was a bit above estimates of 200,000 but didn't do much to alter the real's decline.\par \par \uc2 -By Paulo Winterstein, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11-3544-7073; paulo.winterstein@dowjones.com [ 04-04-12 2008GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120404e8440010z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
